1 DEAT
2 DATE NOV 1259
1 OCCU Archbishop of Trier 1242-1259
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Note: Arnold II of Isenburg (c. 1190–1259) was Archbishop of Trier from 1242 to his death. A long-time member of the cathedral chapter in Trier, he held several provostships before being elected as archbishop, su
2 CONC cceeding his uncle Theoderich von Wied. The election was controversial, and king Conrad IV of Germany granted the regalia to Rudolf de Ponte, the opposing candidate, instead. A short military conflict ensued, and the dispute ended
2 CONC  after Rudolf's death when Arnold was confirmed as archbishop by Pope Innocent IV and consecrated in 1245.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.5em>Arnold opposed Conrad and the Hohenstaufen claim to the throne, and elected Henry Raspe and later William II of Holland as German anti-kings. During his reign, he fortified several towns and built various castles. He died in
2 CONC  Montabaur in early November 1259 and is buried in Trier Cathedral.
2 CONT * Reference: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold_II_of_Isenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
