1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emicho of Leiningen helped lead the German Crusade, 1096. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His relationship to the others is unclear.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emich I was Count of Leiningen in 1127, but it is unclear when he died, or his relation to the other counts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emich II is attested as Count of Leiningen in documents from 1143 to 1179
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich I had taken over the county by 1189
2 CONT
2 CONT Emich III is attested as Count of Leiningen in documents from 1193 through 1208, though it is unclear his relationship to the previous Counts
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich I, cousin of Emich III, was recorded as junior count under Emich in 1205, and as count in his own right from 1210 to 1217. A document from 1220 refers to his widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leiningen_family#Earliest_Counts
