1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Sophie von Andechs-Meranien==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Berthold III., Markgraf, Herzog von Andechs von Andechs, Markgraf von Istrien-Krain and Hedwig von Wittelsbach, Erbin von Neuburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CARINTHIA.htm#SophiaAndechsdied1218 Project MedLands CARINTHIA]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BERTOLD [II] von Andechs, son of BERTOLD [I] Graf von Andechs & his first wife Sophia of Istria''' (-14 Dec 1188, bur Diessen).  "Berhtolfus Comes de Diezzen" donated serfs to Diessen monastery, in the presence of "uxore sua So
2 CONC phia et filiis suis Poppone et Bertolfo"[318].  His parentage is confirmed by the Notæ Diessenses which record the death "1188 XIX Kal Ian" of "Berhtoldus marchio de Andehs…filius Berhtoldi comitis fundatoris nostre ecclesie"[319]
2 CONC .  Graf von Andechs 1147.  A charter dated to [1150] records that "Poppo comes de Gieche" donated property to Admont before leaving for Jerusalem for the soul of "filio suo Heinrico", but that after he died on his expedition "frat
2 CONC er eius Perchtoldus comes" reduced the amount of the donation[320].  Graf von Plassenburg [1158/61].  Graf am unteren Inn 1162.  Graf im Norital and Vogt von Brixen 1166.  He succeeded in 1173 as BERTOLD I Marchese di Istria.  The
2 CONC  Notæ Diessenses record the death "1188 XIX Kal Ian" of "Berhtoldus marchio de Andehs…filius Berhtoldi comitis fundatoris nostre ecclesie" specifying that he was buried "in capitolio"[321]. 
2 CONT '''married  firstly (before 1153) HEDWIG, daughter of --- (-16 Jul 1174, bur Diessen).'''  The Notæ Diessenses record the death "XVII Kal Aug" of "Hadewic comitissa", specifying that she was buried "in capitolio"[322].  The De Fun
2 CONC datoribus Monasterii Diessenses records the death in 1176 of "Hiadwigis uxor eius [=Pertoldi marchio Ystrie]"[323].  The necrology of Diessen records the death "1176 Kal Aug XVII" of "Hadewic com sepulta in capitolio…uxor Berhtold
2 CONC i marchionis"[324].  Her origin is less clear.  Wegener refers to the testament of Friedrich Pfalzgraf von Wittelsbach which names Berthold [II] Graf von Andechs as his near relative and concludes that Hedwig must therefore have b
2 CONC een Friedrich's sister[325], and therefore Hedwig von Wittelsbach, daughter of Otto [IV] Pfalzgraf von Wittelsbach & his wife Heilika von Lengenfeld-Hopfenohe-Pettendorf.  However, there must be other possibilities. 
2 CONT '''married secondly ([1180], divorced) LUITGARD of Denmark, daughter of SVEND III "Grade" King of Denmark & his wife Adelheid von Meissen.'''  The Genealogia Wettinensis names "Lucardem quam duxit Bertoldus marchio de Bavaria" as 
2 CONC daughter of "Adela [von Meissen] [et] regi Danorum Suenoni", noting that they were separated with episcopal consent because of adultery[326]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marchese Bertold & his first wife HEDWIG had four children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''BERTOLD''' (-12 Aug 1204, bur Diessen).  The De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses names "Pertoldus dux Meranie marchio Ystrie…filius Pertoldi marchionis" when recording his death in 1204[327].  He succeeded his fa
2 CONC ther in 1188 as Graf von Andechs.  Marchese of Istria, Duke of Merano. 
2 CONT * 2.        ''' SOPHIA''' (-2 Jan 1218).  The De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses lists (in order) "Poppo summus prepositus Babenberch, Mathildis marchionissa de Hohenburch, Kunigundis comitissa de Eberstein, Sophia comitissa de
2 CONC  Hennenberch, Berhtoldus dux et marchio…"[328], increasing the probability that all were children of "Berhtoldus marchio".  The necrology of Diessen records the death "IV Non Jan" of "Sophia com"[329].  '''married  (before 1182) P
2 CONC OPPO [VI] Graf von Henneberg, son of BERTHOLD [I] Graf von Henneberg Burggraf von Würzburg & his wife Bertha von Putelendorf (-Morgato, Syria 14 Jun [1190]). '''
2 CONT * 3.        ''' KUNIGUNDE''' (-10 Feb after 1207).  The De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses lists (in order) "Poppo summus prepositus Babenberch, Mathildis marchionissa de Hohenburch, Kunigundis comitissa de Eberstein, Sophia co
2 CONC mitissa de Hennenberch, Berhtoldus dux et marchio…"[330], increasing the probability that all were children of "Berhtoldus marchio".  The chronology of the two families suggests [1185/90] as the date of Kunigunde´s marriage.  "Ebe
2 CONC rhardus…dominus de Eberstein…et uxor nostra Chunigunt et filii mei Eberhardus et Otto, Bertholdus et Albertus" donated property to Kloster Herrenalb by charter dated 1207, witnessed by "Cunrado et Godefrido comitibus de Kalwe, com
2 CONC ite Fridrico de Saroponte…"[331].  The necrology of Diessen records the death "IV Id Feb" of "Chunigundis com"[332].  '''married  ([1185/90]) EBERHARD [III] Graf von Eberstein, son of BERTHOLD [IV] [Graf] von Eberstein & his wife 
2 CONC Uta --- (-[1218/19]).''' 
2 CONT * 4.         '''MATHILDE''' (-17 Jan 1245).  The De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses lists (in order) "Poppo summus prepositus Babenberch, Mathildis marchionissa de Hohenburch [error for comitissa Coricie?], Kunigundis comitissa
2 CONC  de Eberstein, Sophia comitissa de Hennenberch, Berhtoldus dux et marchio…"[333], increasing the probability that all were children of "Berhtoldus marchio". The De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses records the death "1245 XVI Kal
2 CONC  Feb" of "Machtildis comitissa Coricie…soror Pertoldi quondam ducis Meranie"[334].  Contessa di Pisino 1222.  '''married ([1190]) as his second wife, ENGELBERT [III] Graf von Görz, son of ENGELBERT [II] Graf von Görz & his wife Ad
2 CONC elheid von Valley [Wittelsbach] (-[1220]).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marchese Bertold & his second wife LUITGARD of Denmark had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 5.         '''POPPO''' (-2 Dec 1245).  The Genealogia Wettinensis names "Popponem Bavenbergensem prepositum et Bertam Gerbestadensem abbatissam" as children of "Lucardem [et] Bertoldus marchio de Bavaria"[335].  The De Fundatori
2 CONC bus Monasterii Diessenses names "Poppo episcopus Babenbergensis…frater Pertoldi quondam ducis Meranie" when recording his death in 1245[336].  Provost of St Jakob 1185/1201.  Provost of St Stephan 1190.  He was elected Bishop of B
2 CONC amberg 1239.  The necrology of Diessen records the death "IV Non Dec" of "Poppo maior ppos Babenbergensis 1245 Bertholdi ducis Meranie"[337]. 
2 CONT * 6.         '''BERTA''' .  The Genealogia Wettinensis names "Popponem Bavenbergensem prepositum et Bertam Gerbestadensem abbatissam" as children of "Lucardem [et] Bertoldus marchio de Bavaria"[338].  Abbess of Gerbstedt bei Eisle
2 CONC ben 1190. 
2 CONT
