2 CONT
2 CONT a)         LUDWIG [I] (-1200 or after).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the second of the two daughters of "Theodoricum de Monte Beliardi" as the mother of "Ludovicus de Salvernia"[425].  Seigneur de Rougemo
2 CONC nt et d'Amance-en-Bourgogne.  "Ludovicus senior comes de Sarwerden" records donations by "avus meus dominus Fridericus comes de Sarwerden et uxor eius Gertrudis…domino Volmaro patre meo et Stephania mea matre…frater meus Ludovicus
2 CONC " to the abbey of Wœrschweiler (Wernereswilre) by charter dated 1172[426].  “Ludowicus...comes de Salwerna” granted toll exemptions in his lands to the monks of Haute-Seille by charter dated 1185[427].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m GERTRUD von Dachsburg, daughter of HEINRICH [I] Graf von Dachsburg & his wife Lutgardis von Sulzbach.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Ludwig [I] & his wife had six children: 
