2 CONT
2 CONT == Helika von Pettendorf==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Friedrich III, Herr von Hopfenoe-Pettendorf-Lengenfeld and Heilika von Staufen 
2 CONT * Heilika of Pettendorf-Lengenfeld (also known as Eilika; c. 1103 – 14 September 1170; buried in Ensdorf Abbey) was by marriage Countess Palatine of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HeilikaPettendorfdied1170 Project MedLands BAVARIAN NOBILITY]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RUOTGER von Feldheim,''' son of --- .  '''married  [EILIKA] von Lengenfeld,''' daughter of FRIEDRICH [I] von Lengenfeld & his wife Sigena von Leige. The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been 
2 CONC identified.   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ruotger & his wife EILIKA von Lengenfeld had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''FRIEDRICH von Pettendorf''' (-3 Apr 1119, bur Kloster Ensdorf).  The Annales Pegavienses name "Ruotgerum Magdeburgensem postea episcopum et Fridericum comitem" as the two sons of "Ruotgerus comes" & his wife, speci
2 CONC fying that the daughter of Friedrich married "Ottoni palatino de Witilinsbach"[2067].  The Fundatio Monasterii Ensdorfensis names "Fridericus pater palatine" in connection with the foundation of Ensdorf[2068] (by his son-in-law Ot
2 CONC to Pfalzgraf von Wittelsbach).  A charter dated 4 Aug 1155 records that “Fridericus pater Palatine et domina Heilwic soror Palatine et Gebehardus maritus eius de Lewkenberge et filii illorum Fridericus et Gebehardus” were buried a
2 CONC t Ensdorf[2069].  '''married  HEILBIRG [Heilwig], daughter of  (-after 1110, bur Kloster Ensdorf).''' The Fundatio Monasterii Ensdorfensis names "Fridericum et Heylwic" as parents of "Heylice palatine", specifying that they were b
2 CONC uried at Ensdorf[2070].  The origin of Heilbirg is not known.  Europäische Stammtafeln[2071] suggests that she was Heilika von Staufen, daughter of Friedrich I Duke of Swabia & his wife Agnes of Germany, although the primary sourc
2 CONC e on which this is based has not yet been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friedrich & his wife HEILBIRG had two children: '''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* i)         ''' HEILIKA von Pettendorf''' (-13 Sep 1170, bur Ensdorf).  The Fundatio Monasterii Ensdorfensis records the death "1170 XVIII Kal Oct" of "Heylice palatine", naming her parents "Fridericum et Heylwic" and specifyi
2 CONC ng that they were all buried at Ensdorf[2072].  The necrology of Undensdorf records the death "XVIII Kal Oct" of "Hailica palatina"[2073].  '''married OTTO [II] Graf von Scheyern Pfalzgraf von Wittelsbach, of OTTO [I] Graf von Sch
2 CONC eyern und Wittelsbach, Pfalzgraf of Bavaria & his wife --- (-4 Aug 1156, bur Ensdorf).'''
2 CONT >>>* ii)        ''' HEILWIG von Pettendorf''' (-before [1166], bur Ensdorf).  The Fundatio Monasterii Ensdorfensis names "domna Heilwic soror palatine" as wife of "Gebehardus…de Leukenberge" in connection with the foundation of En
2 CONC sdorf[2074].  A charter dated 4 Aug 1155 records that “Fridericus pater Palatine et domina Heilwic soror Palatine et Gebehardus maritus eius de Lewkenberge et filii illorum Fridericus et Gebehardus” were buried at Ensdorf[2075].  
2 CONC A charter dated to [1166] records that “Marqwardo de Lewgenberge” donated “predium Wartberch” to Ensdorf for the funeral of “matris sue Heylwic”, refers to earlier donations for the funerals of “mariti sui Gebehardi...Friderici fi
2 CONC lii sui”, and records that “Gebehardus...frater eius” donated property in memory of Marquard who died “in expeditione Friderici Imperatoris apud Longobardos”[2076].   '''married GEBHARD[I] von Leuchtenberg, son of --- (-1146, bur 
2 CONC Kloster Ensdorf).'''
2 CONT * b)         '''RUOTGER (-1126).'''  The Annales Pegavienses name "Ruotgerum Magdeburgensem postea episcopum et Fridericum comitem" as the two sons of "Ruotgerus comes" & his wife[2077].  Archbishop of Magdeburg. 
2 CONT
