1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berthold_II._(Andechs)
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT ******************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold III, Count of Andechs (c. 1110/1122  – November 14, 1188) was the Margrave of Istria as Berthold I from 1173 until 1188. He was the son of Berthold III, Count of Diessen, Plassenberg and Stein (died 1151) and his first wi
2 CONC fe Sophie of Istria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1173, he became the Margrave of Istria after Engelbert III. Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold III was married twice. In 1152 he married Hedwig of Wittelsbach, daughter of Otto IV, Count of Wittelsbach, Count palatine of Bavaria and Heilika of Lengenfeld-Hopfenohe-Pettendorf.[1] They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Berthold IV, Duke of Merania (1153 - 1204).
2 CONT    2. Sophia (died 1218). Married Poppo VI, Count of Henneberg (died c. 1190).
2 CONT    3. Kunigunde (died after 1207). Possibly married Eberhard, Count of Eberstein.
2 CONT    4. Matilda, Countess of Pisino (died 1245). Married Berthold, Margrave of Vohburg. In c. 1190 married secondly Engelbert III, Count of Gorizia (died 1217/20).
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife became in c. 1180 princess Luitgard of Denmark, daughter of king Sweyn III of Denmark and Adela of Meissen. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Poppo, Bishop of Bamberg (died December 2, 1245).
2 CONT    2. Berta, Abbess in Gerbstadt (died 1190).
