2 CONT Otto I, Duke of Merania
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Otto II, Count of Burgundy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto I was Duke of Andechs and Merania and was born, in 1180, to Berthold IV von Dießen, Duke of Andechs and Merania, and Agnes of Lower-Lusatia. He was also Otto II, Count Palatine of Burgundy by his marriage to Beatrice II of Bu
2 CONC rgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of his father, in 1204, Otto became Duke of Andechs and Merania; he became Count of Burgundy on his marriage to Beatrice of Burgundy in 1208.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Beatrice's death in 1231, he ceased to be Count and was succeeded by his son, Otto III.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Otto I's death in 1234, he was further succeeded by his son as Duke of Andechs and Merania.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Beatrice produced the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto, (1226-19 June 1248 at Burg Niesten), who succeeded both his parents in their domains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes, who married firstly Frederick II, Duke of Austria, and secondly Ulrich III, Duke of Carinthia
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix, who married Hermann II, Count of Orlamünde
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, who married Přemysl von Mähren and Frederick, Count of Truhendingen
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide, who succeeded her brother upon his death without children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth, who married Friedrich III, Burgrave of Nuremberg
