1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#HugoIXDagsburgdiedafter1137B
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         ALBERT [II] (-1212).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   Graf von Dachsburg 1175.  "Albertus comes de Dagesberge…" witnessed the charter dated 1192 under which "Henricus…dux L
2 CONC otharingiæ" granted freedoms to "burgensibus…de Filfordia"[296].  "Henricus dux Lotharingiæ et marchio et…Luduicus comes de Lon" agreed to divide "terram de Mussal" if "comes de Dasborc" died without heirs by charter dated 1197[29
2 CONC 7].  "Adelbertus…comes Metensis et de Dasbourch" appointed "nepotem meum ducem Lotharingiæ" as his heir "de castro meo Dasbourgh et abbatia de Hessen, de castro Gerbaden, abbatia de Altorf, de castro de Drotein, de castro Albapai,
2 CONC  de abbatia et advocatia de Herbreheym…comitatu et advocatia…de Metis…allodium de Musal et Waleve"[298].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines in 1211 records the death of "Albertus comes Dasburgensis et domnus de Musal"[29
2 CONC 9].   m GERTRUD von Baden, daughter of HERMANN IV Markgraf von Baden & his second wife Udalhildis --- (-before 30 Mar 1225).  Her parentage and marriage are indicated by the charter dated 1226 under which "Hermannus et Henricus fr
2 CONC atres…Marchiones de Baden" donated property inherited from "neptem nostram Gertrudim comitissam bonæ memoriæ filiam comitis Alberti de Tagisburc" to Strasbourg church[300].  From a chronological point of view, her father must have
2 CONC  been Markgraf Hermann IV if she belonged to the family of the Markgrafen von Baden, assuming the birth of her daughter Gertrud is correctly dated to [1205/06].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identifi
2 CONC ed.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          HEINRICH (-Andain 1202).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   He was killed in a tournament[301]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         WILHELM (-Andain 1202).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   He was killed in a tournament[302]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        GERTRUD ([May 1205/mid-1206]-before 19 Mar 1225).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names ...
