1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkmontb.htm#EtiennetteMontbeliardMFolmarSaarwerden v4.2 Updated 07 February 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT HIERRY de Mousson, son of THIERRY de Mousson & his wife Ermentrude de Bourgogne [Comté] ([1076/78]-[mid-Jan] 1163).  "Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus" founded the Cl
2 CONC uniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone"[1].  He inherited his families territories along t
2 CONC he Meuse valley in 1103.  He was expelled by his Meuse subjects in [1113] because of his intolerable behaviour, and transferred to the county of Montbéliard: the Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Theodericus" as broth
2 CONC er of "Raynaldum…comes Barri et Montionis" specifying that Thierry was expelled in 1113 and retained only the county of Montbéliard[2].  Comte de Montbéliard.  Etienne Bishop of Metz declared that “frater meus Teodericus comes de 
2 CONC Montbiliart” recognised the incorrectness of his claims relating to Gorze Abbey by charter dated to [1138/63], naming “cognati nostri Theoderic, Mettensis primicerii”[3].  A charter dated to [1145] confirms the donations to Belcha
2 CONC mp abbey by "dominus Theodericus comes de Monte Beligardis", with the consent of "Theoderici filii sui"[4].  Humbert Archbishop of Besançon confirmed the foundation of Grâce-Dieu abbey by “dominus Theobaldus de Rubeo Monte et domi
2 CONC nus Richardus de Montefalcone...assensu uxorum suarum atque filiorum suorum”, in the presence of “...Theodoricus comes de Monte Belli Cordis...”, by charter dated “V Non Mai” 1147[5].  "Theodericus comes de Monte Biligardis" donat
2 CONC ed toll revenues to numerous abbeys, after the death of "Theoderici filii mei", by charter dated 1160[6].  His death, and that of his son, are recorded in 1163 and before 1160 respectively in the necrology of the abbey of Saint-Pi
2 CONC erre le Vif, Sens, where their supposed ancestor Louis died [1016/25][7]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Thierry's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Thierry & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         ETIENNETTE de Montbéliard (-after 4 Dec 1160).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the second of the two daughters of "Theodoricum de Monte Beliardi" as the mother of "Ludovicus de Salvernia"[10].  H
2 CONC er name is confirmed by the charter dated 1172 under which her son "Ludovicus senior comes de Sarwerden" records donations by "avus meus dominus Fridericus comes de Sarwerden et uxor eius Gertrudis…domino Volmaro patre meo et Step
2 CONC hania mea matre…frater meus Ludovicus" to the abbey of Wœrschweiler (Wernereswilre)[11].  m FOLMAR von Saarwerden, son of FRIEDRICH [I] Graf von Saarwerden & his wife Gertrud --- (-1165 or after).  He took part in the Second Crusa
2 CONC de, returning before 10 Aug 1149 when he is recorded at Varangéville[12]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT .''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#FolmarSaarwerdendied1165 v4.1 Updated 29 April 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Folmar & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         LUDWIG [I] (-1200 or after).  
2 CONT *b)         LUDWIG [II] (-after 1172). 
