1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMBURG.htm#Sophiedied1226 v4.3 Updated 15 February 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT SOPHIE van Limburg (-[1226/27]).  Levoldus’s mid-14th century Chronica Comitum de Marka records that “Fredericus comes de Hysenberch” married “sororem Henrici ducis Limburgensis”[183].  Her parentage is confirmed by the charter da
2 CONC ted 1242 under which her son "Theodericus dominus de Isenberg" declared having surrendered "allodium castri…Limburg supra Lenan" to "domino et avunculo meo Henrico comite de Monte", and having been regranted it as a fief[184].  A 
2 CONC charter dated 24 Aug 1244 also confirms her parentage, recording that "Theoderici filii sororis ducis de Lymborch" renewed his allegiance to "domini Henrici ducis de Lymborch et comitis de Monte" for the recently constructed "cast
2 CONC ro Lynborch"[185].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.   The Continuatio of the Chronicon Lamberti Parvi records the death in 1225 of "Galerannus dux Ardennæ et filia eius uxor Frederici prodit
2 CONC oris ludificatione dæmonum cum parvulo filio"[186].  m ([1210]) FRIEDRICH [II] Graf von Altena und Isenberg, son of ARNOLD Graf von Altena und Hövel & his wife Mechtild --- (-Köln 14 Nov 1226). 
