1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ida von Lummen von Limburg (born von Chiny)    ------ van is von
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1180
2 CONT Death:
2 CONT Father:     Lord Lodewijk 11,  van Chiny [Translates Ludwig von Chiny] - viscount of Verdun 
2 CONT Mother:    Ide Chiny (born de Rumigny)
2 CONT Husband: Frederik von Limburg (advocate of Hesbaye)
2 CONT Daughter: Mathilde von Limburg (born von Lummen)           Limburg is Lummen I think???
2 CONT
2 CONT GOOGLED correction as Initially Profiled as: "N.N. de Chiny, vrouwe van Lummen"
2 CONT ANSWER:  (likely Ida van Chiny) was a 12th-century noblewoman born around 1180. She was the daughter of Lodewijk II van Chiny (viscount of Verdun and lord of Lummen) and Ide de Rumigny. She married Frederik van Limburg (advocate o
2 CONC f Hesbaye), with whom she had a daughter, Mathilde van Limburg (vrouwe van Lummen).Would you like to know more about the descendants of the house of Lummen or the Limburg-Chiny lineage?
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Ludwig von Chiny, Herr zu Lummen, Vogt des Haspengaues2,3 d. 1207 Mother: (Miss) de Rumigny 4,3
2 CONT (Miss) von Lummen married Friedrich von Lummen, Vogt von St. Lambert zu Luttich, son of Heinrich III, Duke of Limbourg, Graf von Arlon, Sheriff of Klosterrath and Adelheid von Henneberg.2,3 Family Friedrich von Lummen, Vogt von St
2 CONC . Lambert zu Luttich d. bt Apr 1211 - May 1212 Child	 Mathilde von Limburg+2,5 d. a 1261
2 CONT
