1 NAME Gerard van Limburg, Herr von Wassenberg
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1215
1 DEAT
2 DATE SEP 1254
1 OCCU Count of Wassenburg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT From Medlands, retrieved 18 April 2022:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMBURG.htm#GerhardIVWassenbergdied1255 GERHARD] [III] van Limburg (-5 or 7 Dec 1225, bur Wassenberg). m (before 1212) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMBURG.htm#BeatrixMerheimMGerhardWassenberg 
2 CONC BEATRIX] von Merheim, daughter of RUTGER von Merheim & his wife Aleidis von Bemelen (-after 1242).   Gerhard & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)         [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMBURG.htm#GerhardIVWassenbergdied1255 GERHARD] [IV] von Wassenberg (-[10 Mar/Sep] 1255).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly BEATRIX von Randerode, daughter of GERHARD [II] Herr von Randerode und Liedberg & his wife --- (-before 2 Feb 1246).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified. Gerhard [IV]
2 CONC  & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT *(a)       GERHARD [V] von Wassenberg (-[13 Mar 1253/1255]).  Walram IV Duke of Limburg noted, in a charter dated 13 Mar 1253, that "nobilis vir Gerardus dominus de Wassenberg" had granted "castrum de Spremont" to "dominæ Elisabet
2 CONC h uxori suæ, sorori…Henric…quondam ducis Brabantiæ", with the consent of "Gerardi primogeniti sui"[143].  The date of this charter indicates that Gerhard [V] must have been born from his father’s first marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (contract 19 Mar 1247) as her second husband, [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRABANT,%20LOUVAIN.htm#Elisabethdied1272 ELISABETH] de Brabant, widow of DIETRICH von Kleve gt von Dinslaken, daughter of HENRI I Duke of Br
2 CONC abant & his second wife Marie de France (-[22 Jan 1260/14 Aug 1266]). Gerhard & his second wife had two children:
2 CONT *(b)       JUTTA von Wassenberg (-after 25 Nov 1258).  "Elisabet domina de Sprimont" granted "Mirmekar" to "Jutta filia nostra", stated to be a minor, with the consent of "Ottoni comiti Gelriæ", by charter dated 25 Nov 1258[144]. 
2 CONT *(c)       GERHARD von Wassenberg ([1254/55]-before 14 Oct 1257).  "Elisabeth domina de Sprimunth, comitissa Cleven relicta nobilis viri domini de Wassenberg" donated revenue to Rolduc [Rode] abbey, for the souls of "prenominati d
2 CONC omini nostri Gerardi, eiusdem nominis filii nostri", by charter dated 14 Oct 1257[145].  This appears to be a different person from Gerhard [V], son of Gerhard [IV], who is named above.  If Gerhard [V] had been born from his fathe
2 CONC r´s second marriage, it is likely that he would have been considered too young to have confirmed his father´s transaction dated 13 Mar 1253.  In addition, the 1253 charter refers to Gerhard [V] as "primogeniti sui", referring to h
2 CONC is father, not "primogeniti nostri".  It is assumed, therefore, that Gerhard [V] died soon after the 1253 charter and that Gerhard [IV]´s second wife gave birth to a sonwh was given the same name shortly before the death of her hu
2 CONC sband.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kasteel_Limbricht
