1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIA.htm#Wiltrudisdied1093<br/>
2 CONT 5.         WILTRUDIS (-1093, bur Hirsau).  The Historia Hirsaugiensis Monasterii names "Wieldrude" as wife of "Adalberti de Kalwa" but does not give her origin[316].  The Codex Hirsaugiensis records that “Adalbertus comes senior d
2 CONC e Kalwa” gave numerous properties to Hirsau with the consent of “uxore sua Wielicha filiisque suis Brunone, Adalberto, Gotefrido ac filiabus Uta et Irmingarde”[317].  The Chronicon of Bernold records the death in 1093 of "uxor com
2 CONC itis Adelberti…Weliga, magni ducis Gotifredi filia" and her burial "apud Hyrsaugiense monasterium"[318].  The Codex Hirsaugiensis records that “Adalbertus comes senior de Kalwa” later gave property “ad Scaltebrunnen” to Hirsau “pr
2 CONC o coniuge Wielicha et...pro filio Adalberto”, suggesting that both had predeceased the donor[319].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ADALBERT Graf von Calw, son of ADALBERT [I] Graf im Ufgau & his wife Adelheid von Egisheim (-Hirsau 22 Sep 1099, bur Hirsau).  
