1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Elisabeth von Anhalt-Wildberg==
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT * Burgrave Poppo VII was the only son of Burgrave Poppo VI. and Sophia von Andechs-Meranien. His first marriage was to Elisabeth von Anhalt-Wildberg, daughter of Berthold von Wildberg (approx. 1165-1233) and Sophia von Auhausen (1
2 CONC 180-1220).
2 CONT * [http://www.manfred-hiebl.de/genealogie-mittelalter/henneberg/poppo_7_graf_1245/poppo_7_1245.html Poppo VII] followed in 1191 together with his brothers Otto II and Berthold II , shared with Otto II in 1212and became Count von H
2 CONC enneberg . Under him the conflict with the bishops of Würzburg broke out incurably. In 1220/21 he tried to succeed his nephew Berthold III. to take on what was refused. In the end he gave up this already largely hollowed-out castl
2 CONC e office, lost important episcopal fiefs such as Mellrichstädt, Stockheim and Meiningen, and became an episcopal vassal for other properties, such as Untermaßfeld.The dispute intensified because of the inheritance Botenlauben, the
2 CONC  property of the brother, and the episcopal attempt, the Henneberger Encircle the main allodes by building castles. The office of Lichtenberg was lost to the Fulda Abbey, for which he was given other areas as fiefs; The relationsh
2 CONC ip with Fulda remained quite peaceful over the centuries. He moved the residence to Schleusingen, which was beyond the control of the bishops of Würzburg and promoted this place very much. The conflict - also with other neighbors 
2 CONC - was ultimately rooted in everyone's efforts to enforce the territorialization of their rulers; the lords of Hallenberg became vassals. With his second marriage, he temporarily relieved Thuringia's pressure on Henneberg. Like his
2 CONC  ancestors, he was a loyal supporter ofSTAUFER, was heavily involved in imperial politics, took part against Egypt in 1217/18 and with Kaiser in 1228/29FREDERICK II to Jerusalem. He was co-regent in Austria from 1237-1239, quarrel
2 CONC ed with the HENNEBERGER branch lines Wasungen and Frankenstein , won allodies from these and was heavily indebted through his many feuds.   1. oo'''ELISABETH VON WILDBERG†around 1220'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * From 1191 until his death he was Vogt of Maria Bildhausen Monastery. 1212 took over the office of the burgrave of Würzburg. In 1235 he bequeathed his fiefdom in Ezzelshausen to the Würzburg monastery so that the new Maidbronn mo
2 CONC nastery could be built at this point . The burgrave office opened up important room for maneuver for the Hennebergers as the most important secular power in northern Franconia , but also brought them all too often into conflict wi
2 CONC th the Bishopric of Würzburg , because since 1168 was by Emperor Friedrich Barbarossasecular power and ecclesiastical power combined and the age of the prince-bishops began.
2 CONT * Babenberger - https://wuerzburgwiki.de/wiki/Babenberger
2 CONT * List of the Würzburg canons - https://wuerzburgwiki.de/wiki/Liste_der_W%C3%BCrzburger_Domherren
2 CONT * County of Henneberg - https://wuerzburgwiki.de/wiki/Grafschaft_Henneberg
2 CONT * Secular rulers - https://wuerzburgwiki.de/wiki/Weltliche_Herrscher
2 CONT * Manfred Geneology - http://www.manfred-hiebl.de/genealogie-mittelalter/henneberg/poppo_7_graf_1245/poppo_7_1245.html
2 CONT * B randenburg Erich: The Descendants of Charlemagne Verlag Degener & Co Neustadt an der Aisch 1998 Plate 36 Page 74 - L utz, Wolf Rudolf: Heinrich der Erlauchte (1218-1288 ) Margrave of Meissen and the Ostmark (1221-1288) Landgra
2 CONC ve of Thuringia and Count Palatine of Saxony (1247-1263), publisher Palm & Enke Erlangen - P atze Hans / Sch Lesinger Walter: history of Thuringia page 203 - Sch wennicke Detlev: European Stammtafeln New episode Volume I. 1, Vitto
2 CONC rio Klostermann GmbH Frankfurt am Main 1998 Plate 145 - Sch Wennicke, Detlef:European family tables. Family tables on the history of the European states. New series Volume XVI, Bavaria and Franconia Plate 144 - Th iele Andreas: Na
2 CONC rrative genealogical STAMMTABELN on European history Volume I, Part 1 Plate 173,174 - W eller Tobias: The marriage policy of the German high nobility in the 12th century page 623,675,718,721 
