3 TEXT Albrecht II of Austria (* December 12 1298 in the Habsburg ( Aargau ), † August 16 1358 in Vienna , he was buried in the which he founded Gaming Charterhouse , called the Wise or lame ) was Duke of Austria .
4 CONT Table of Contents  [ Hide ] 
4 CONT One life
4 CONT 2 Marriage and issue
4 CONT 3 Literature
4 CONT 4 links
4 CONT 5 Notes and references
4 CONT Life [ Edit ]
4 CONT
4 CONT Albrecht II, called the Wise or lame, was the son of the Roman-German King Albrecht I 12 Born in December 1298. Originally intended for holy orders, he became in 1313 a minor into by individual canons in questionable choice Passau
4 CONC  Bishops elected, but came in conflict with the Gegenelekten Gebhard of Walsee in a stalemate, had in 1317 finally renounce and turned away from the spiritual path. [1] He reached jointly with his younger brother Otto in 1330 to t
4 CONC he government of all Habsburgian countries. This he increased by the goods of his wife Johanna ( Pfirt county and some cities).
4 CONT Albrecht also put his claims to Carinthia against John of Bohemia through: After the death of Henry of Carinthia , Emperor Ludwig the Bavarian brothers Otto and Albert on 2 May 1335 in Linz areas Carinthia and the southern part of
4 CONC  Tyrol as a fief . Albrecht's reputation proves the fact that it not only Pope Benedict XII. asked in 1335 to mediate reconciliation with Emperor Louis the Church, but also King Philip VI. France from 1337 to his aid against Emper
4 CONC or Louis and King Edward of England asked.
