1 NOTE {geni:about_me} a)      '''   JOHANN [II]''' (-17 Dec 1380).  '''Graf von Laufenburg'''.  “Frau Agnes Gräfin von Habsburg und die Grafen Johannes, Rudolf u. Gotfrid v. H. Ihre Söhne” witnessed the charter dated 24 Jun 1347 which r
2 CONC ecords an agreement between the abbess of Seckingen and the fishermen of Laufenburg[291].  Landgraf im Sisgau.  Graf von Habsburg-Neurapperswil 1353.  The necrology of Wettingen records the death "XVI Kal Jan 1380" of "Iohannes co
2 CONC m de Habsburg"[292]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her second husband, VERENA de Neuchâtel, 
2 CONT '''widow''' of RODOLPHE [III] de Neuchâtel Seigneur de Nidau, 
2 CONT daughter of THIEBAUT [V] Seigneur de Neuchâtel [en Bourgogne] & his wife Agnes von Geroldseck (-1372).  Her family origin and her two marriages are indicated by a charter dated 21 Sep 1352 under which [her son] “Graff Rudolf von N
2 CONC uwenburg herre ze Nydow” appointed Louis Comte de Neuchâtel to arbitrate disputes with “Verenen von Nuwenburg graevinen ze Habspurg, min muoter”, naming “graff Peter herren ze Arberg, minen vetter”[293].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Graf Johann [II] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT *i)          VERENA .  <br> '''m''' firstly (9 Sep 1354) as his second wife, FILIPPINO Gonzaga, son of LODOVICO [I] Gonzaga Podestà di Mantua & his first wife Richilda --- (-5 Apr 1356). <br> '''m''' secondly BURCHARD [XI] Graf vo
2 CONC n Hohenberg Herr von Nagold, son of OTTO [II] Graf von Hohenberg [Hohenzollern] gt von Nagold & his first wife Kunigunde von Wertheim. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *ii)         JOHANN [III] (-11 Jan 1392).  Graf von Laufenburg.  Herr zu Rotenberg 1389.  The necrology of Wettingen records the death "III Id Jan 1392" of "Iohannes com filius quondam domini Iohannis de Habsburg"[294]. 
2 CONT
