3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Heer van Geich, Obergeich, Konzendorf, Schlich en Horn - Koninklijk minister, Heer van Echts, Merode, Geich, Konzendof, Schlich en Horn
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} April 1174 in the wake of Emperor Frederick Barbarossa, appears until 25.10.1855 in a document. Before 1174 he is entrusted with the administration of the court belonging to Reichsgut Echtz. Werner has a castle sea
2 CONC t built on a clearing, after which he and his descendants call themselves "van me Rode" or "de Rode".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gedbas.genealogy.net/person/show/1134962843
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/tinyscholten?lang=nl&pz=tiny&nz=scholten&p=adelheid&n=rode+van&type=fiche
2 CONT
2 CONT mentions that he could have been the son of Adelheid van Rode, daughter of Hugo van Rode and king Pedro Berenger of Aragon. This seems unlikely, as the birth year of Adelheid appears to be definitely some 40 years after that of We
2 CONC rner I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before the 12th century, there was in that region south west of the lower Rhine river only the great 'Oedenrode' named after St. Oda before 800). When Werner built his castle , Oedenrode must have sounded as 'Oudenrode', - 'The ol
2 CONC d Rode'. He had the intention to build a new Rode, 'Nierode', which, in handwriting, can be easily read as 'Merode'.
2 CONT
2 CONT The explanation 'van me Rode' has actually no plausible semantic base and seems very 'ad hoc'....but time will tell..
