2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold_V,_Count_of_Looz Arnold V, Count of Looz Marriage and family[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married June 21, 1280 Marguerite Vianden († 1316), Lady of Perwez and Grimbergen, daughter of Philip I, Count of Vianden, and Marie de Louvain, and had: Louis IV († 1336), Count of Loon and Chiny,[6] Jean, who died young, Arnol
2 CONC d, Mathilde (1282 † 1313), married to Godefroy II, Lord of Heinsberg, Blankenberge and WASSEMBERG (1331), in which she dowry Fortress Vogelsanck (the current town of Heusden-Zolder, Belgium Limburg) with areas of Zwilre, Sonhoven 
2 CONC and Hautaets and parent Thierry Heinsberg, Count of Loon and Chiny, Mary, married first husband Gilles Berthout, confessed Mechelen, died childless in 1310; she married second husband Gerard Diest, lord of Antwerp; she dies withou
2 CONC t children shortly after.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne, lady Quaetbeke, Arnulf of widow Wesemael, lord of Bergen op Zom of Woude and Quaetbeke, died around 1312; she then married William of Oreye, to be lord of Rummen (Rumigny) by donation of Louis IV of Loon in 1331 Margaret, 
2 CONC wife of William de Duras, told of Neufchatel, Esquire; his father gave him as dowry the castle and lordship of Duras; as he survives his half-brothers Counts of Chiny, it brings it to his possessions county, and in 1299 added to h
2 CONC is titles that of Count of Chiny.
2 CONT
