2 CONT
2 CONT A Oberdorf, Grentzingen village depended on the parish level, we find at the end of the seventeenth century Jean-Jacques ORTSCHEID, the clerk of the village. During the baptism of his daughter [http://www.geni.com/people/Marie-d-O
2 CONC rtscheid/6000000026208391915?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1450652523079&through=6000000037893584292 Mary Elisabeth] Maybe the same as this other [http://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth-Saltzman/6000000037893584292?from_flash=1&fsession_
2 CONC id=1450650287813&through=6000000038768724131 (Mary?) Elizabeth] in '''*1683''', he was called "Domini," that is to say "Sir", which is related to its function. At baptism mentioned, the godfather was Jean-Georges ORTSCHEID Altkirc
2 CONC h who lived where he was a prosecutor tax. He was assigned around 1696 the following arms. "azure door three spikes money badly ordered" Jean-Georges died in 1719 in Altkirch at the age of 77 ('''75?''') years altkirchoise.
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Marie Elisabeth was Baptized in "MAY 20 1684 in the village of Habsheim (not Oberdorf), 68440, Haut Rhin, Alsace, FRANCE'' - Could it be, either a mistake of the chronicler or was there another Mary Elisabeth born in 1683- ''do
2 CONC ubtful''
