1 NAME Heinrich /von Schönrode/
2 GIVN Heinrich
2 _MARNM von Schönrode
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 18 FEB 1356
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From German Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich von Schönrode (Heynrich van Schöynroyde) was a knight in the 14th century, he was married to Lysa, née von Stummel. The marriage produced at least one child, the son Reinald von Schönrode. [1] The von Schöynerode family (
2 CONC Schoenrath, Schonrod) named themselves after the knight's seat of the same name Schönrath Castle [2] in the Rhein-Sieg district , and is recorded in 1374 as living at the Altenberger Hof near Mülheim a. Rhine resident is mentioned
2 CONC  and occurs repeatedly in the history of the Bergisches Land .
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 18, 1356, the "Vowynkele" estate (today Wuppertal - Vohwinkel ) was sold by Heinrich von Schönrode to the Gräfrath monastery near Solingen . This document is considered the first written mention of Vohwinkel and is the
2 CONC  oldest document in the Wuppertal city archives .
2 CONT
2 CONT The wording of the document dated February 18, 1356:
2 CONT
2 CONT there a number of other frontierghe still anes praghe ze doyne and the vorscreven (above mentioned) erfs and goyts werschaf zo doyn as boven end beneden (above and below, as much as everywhere) ghewoynlich is in the county of the 
2 CONC Berghe. This is schyet (happened) before Dyederighe Smende vayde (vogt) zo Solinghen, Hermanne van Lymlynchoven syne dinghere (perhaps court messenger), Tyelen zum turne (the street at the tower in Sonnborn is still reminiscent of
2 CONC  this; turn - tower) and Nolden up the byse scheffenen zo Sunburne, Johanne vam graven, Willame van Schlugheym, Johanne deme Wymanne and Henken syme sone. In orc and dis bryefs so hayn I presented to Heynrich. myn ynghesigel an de
2 CONC men bryef ghehanghen vor mir end myne vorghenoemde (above mentioned) vrouw Lyse. Finally I tell Lysa. (aforementioned) be kenne dis verzyghenisse (renunciation) under sygele Heynrichs myns mans vorg.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Date sub anno domini M CCC quinquagesimo sexto decima octava the mensis februarij.
2 CONT In a more understandable form the text reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT “I - Heinrich von Schönrode, knight, and Lisa, my married housewife, make known to all those who see, hear about and read this letter that we are speaking together for ourselves and our heirs directly through this letter before th
2 CONC e lay judge and the bailiff of SonnbornTo renounce with hand and mouth the entire inheritance and property in Vohwinkel, which is located in the Sonnborn parish, with all its accessories, which was ours and which we sold with sati
2 CONC sfaction to the honorable spiritual monastery of Gräfrath for a fixed sum of money is well paid to us in cash and to our will, there is no other demand or claim to the aforementioned inheritance and property management, as is usua
2 CONC l everywhere in the county of the mountain. This happened in front of Diedrich Smende, Vogt zu Solingen, Hermann von Limlichhoven, his servant, Thielen zum Turne and Nolden on the beise, Alderman zu Sonnborn, Johann vom Graben, Wi
2 CONC lhelm von Schlagheim, Johann the Weimann and Henken, his son. To certify this letter, I, Heinrich, have my seal attached to this letter for me and my aforementioned wife Lisa. And I, the aforementioned Lisa, confess this renunciat
2 CONC ion under the seal of Heinrich, my aforementioned husband, because I do not have my own seal at the moment.
2 CONT
2 CONT – During the year of the Lord 1356 on the 18th day of the month of February.
