2 CONT '''Godefroi (Godfrey II)''' "Duke of Lower Lotharingia & Louvain" de Louvain formerly Lorraine Born about 1107 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfrey II was the Count of Leuven, Landgrave of Brabant by inheritance from 23 January 1139. He was also the Duke of Lower Lorraine (as Godfrey VII), and as such also Margrave of Antwerp, by appointment in 1139 after the death of
2 CONC  Duke Waleran.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was first associated with his father in 1136, when he first carried the ducal title. This was confirmed by Conrad III of Germany, who had married the sister of Godfrey's wife. Waleran left a son, Henry II of Limburg, who assert
2 CONC ed his father's ducal rights. Godfrey and Henry entered into a war in which the latter was decisively and quickly destroyed. Godfrey did not long enjoy his victory. He was killed by a disease of the liver two years thence. He was 
2 CONC buried in St. Peter's Church in Leuven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors  Son of Godefroi (Louvain) de Louvain and Ida (Chiny) de Louvain  Brother of Adeliza (Brabant) of Louvain, Ida de Lorraine and Joscelin (Leuven) Percy [half]  Husband of Luitgarde (Sulzbach) van Leuven — married [date un
2 CONC known] [location unknown]  Descendants  Father of Godefroi (Lorraine) of Leuven  Died 13 Jun 1142 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfrey II (Lorraine) de Louvain is a member of royalty, nobility or aristocracy in Europe. Join: European Royals and Aristocrats 742-1499 Project Discuss: euroaristo Biography He was the oldest son. He succeeded his father in 113
2 CONC 9. Shortly before he had married Lutgart von Sulzbach, the sister in law of king Conrad III. Relatively little is known of him, as he died in 1142, leaving behind only a son a less then a year old.  Occupation  Count of Louvain; D
2 CONC uke of Lower Lorraine; Margrave of Antwerp 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Gottfried IV. (Niederlothringen) Gottfried IV., genannt der Bucklige (* um 1040; † 27. Februar 1076) war Herzog von Niederlothringen von 1069 bis 1076. Er war ein Sohn Herzog Gottfrieds III. von Niederlothringen und seiner Ehefrau
2 CONC  Doda. Er wurde 1069 aus politischen Erwägungen mit Mathilde von Tuszien verheiratet, der Tochter des Markgrafen Bonifatius IV. von Tuszien und der Beatrix von Bar, die ihrerseits als Witwe Gottfrieds Vater geheiratet hatte. Gottf
2 CONC ried IV. und Mathilde hatten nur ein Kind, Beatrix († 1071). Ab 1071 lebte das Paar getrennt, im Investiturstreit stand Mathilde auf der Seiten von Papst Gregor VII. (Guelfen), Gottfried hingegen auf der des Königs Heinrich IV. (G
2 CONC hibellinen). Gottfried IV. kämpfte 1075 bei Homburg an der Unstrut im Sachsenkrieg für den König gegen den Herzog Magnus von Sachsen. Zusammen mit Wilhelm, Bischof von Utrecht, vertrieb er Graf Dietrich V. aus West-Friesland, dem 
2 CONC späteren Holland. 1076 wurde er in Vlaardingen ermordet, im Auftrag von Dietrich V. und dessen Stiefvater Graf Robert I. von Flandern. Da er ohne Nachkommen war, hatte er gegen den Widerstand Mathildes, seinen Neffen Gottfried von
2 CONC  Bouillon zum Nachfolger bestimmt. In der folgenden Erbauseinandersatzung bestimmte dann der Kaiser seinen jüngeren Sohn Konrad zum Herzog, Graf Albert III. von Namur wurde als vicedux (Vizeherzog) und Regent bestimmt. Gottfried v
2 CONC on Bouillon konnte sein Erbe erst 1088 antreten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gottfried_IV._(Niederlothringen)
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT English http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godfrey_IV,_Duke_of_Lower_Lorraine
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Godfrey II of Leuven
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfrey II (c. 1110 – 13 June 1142) was the count of Leuven, landgrave of Brabant by inheritance from 23 January 1139. He was the son of Godfrey I and Ida of Chiny. He was also the duke of Lower Lorraine (as Godfrey VII), and as s
2 CONC uch also margrave of Antwerp, by appointment in 1139 after the death of Duke Waleran.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was first associated with his father in 1136, when he first carried the ducal title. This was confirmed by Conrad III of Germany, who had married the sister of Godfrey's wife. Waleran left a son, Henry II of Limburg, who assert
2 CONC ed his father's ducal rights. Godfrey and Henry entered into a war in which the latter was decisively and quickly destroyed. Godfrey did not long enjoy his victory. He was killed by a disease of the liver two years thence. He was 
2 CONC buried in St. Peter's Church in Leuven.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Luitgarde, daughter of Berengar I of Sulzbach and sister of Gertrude von Sulzbach, wife of Conrad III of Germany, and Bertha, wife of Manuel I Comnenus, the emperor of Byzantium. He was succeeded by his son Godfrey III 
2 CONC in both the counties and the duchy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source (obsolete): Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Line 155-24.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dupréel, E. (1904) ''Histoire Critique de Godefroi le Barbu, Duc de Lotharingie, Marquis de Toscane''. Uccle, Belgium: Imprimerie-lithographie F. Wauters. Available at: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Histoire_critique_de_Go
2 CONC defroi_le_Barbu_d/zDAbAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0 Google Books]. 2018 Reprint ISBN: 9780270587579 ([https://www.amazon.com/Histoire-Critique-Godefroi-Lotharingie-Marquis/dp/0270587578/ref=tmm_pap_swatch_0?_encoding=UTF8&qid=&sr= Amazon]
2 CONC .
