2 CONT * '''Enumerates him "Godfrey VII.:'''
2 CONT * '''In 1033,''' the two duchies were reunited. Upon the death of Gothelon I, they were separated again.
2 CONT ** 1044-1046: Gothelon II the Dodgy, son of the preceding, deposed by Emperor Henry III (son of Conrad the Salic)
2 CONT **  1046-1065: Frederick IV of Luxembourg (1003-1065), second cousin of Gothelon I
2 CONT **  1065-1069: Godfrey II the Bearded (died 1069), son of Gothelon I (former Duke of Upper Lotharingia)
2 CONT **  1069-1076: Godfrey III the Hunchback (died 1076), son of the preceding
2 CONT **  1076-1089: Conrad II, son of Emperor Henry IV (son of Henry III)
2 CONT **  Vice-Duke: Albert III of Namur (great-grandson of Duke Charles I)
2 CONT **  1089-1096: Godfrey IV of Bouillon (died 1100) nephew of Godfrey III the Hunchback, went on crusade in 1096: advocate of the Holy Sepulchre.
2 CONT **  1101-1106: Henry I of Limburg (died 1118), Duke of Limburg, grandson of Frederick of Luxembourg
2 CONT **  1106-1125: Godfrey V the Courageous (1060-1140), Count of Louvain (Godfrey I)
2 CONT **  1125-1138: Waleran of Limburg (died 1139), son of Henry I of Limburg
2 CONT **  1138-1140: Godfrey V the Courageous, restored (1060-1140), Count of Louvain and Landgrave of Brabant
2 CONT **  1140-1143: Godfrey VI (died 1143), Count of Louvain (Godfrey II), '''son of the above''', Landgrave of Brabant and Duke of Lower Lotharingia
2 CONT **  '''1143-1190: Godfrey VII, Landgrave of Brabant and last Duke of Lower Lotharingia, son of the previous one.'''
