2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gertrude_of_Baden
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude of Baden (before 1160 – before 1225) was a Margravine of Baden by birth and by marriage a Countess of Dagsburg. She was a daughter of Margrave Hermann III of Baden and his wife, Bertha of Tübingen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude married in 1180 to Albert II of Dagsburg (d. 1211). With him she had two sons, Henry and William, and a daughter, Gertrude (d. 1225). Both sons were killed in a tournament in Andain in 1202, so that the noble family of th
2 CONC e Etichonids died out in the male line with Albert II in 1211. This left her daughter Gertrude as heiress of the county of Dagsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her daughter Gertrude married in 1215 in her first marriage to Duke Theobald I of Lorraine. In 1217, she married her second husband, Count Theobald IV of Champagne, who was also King of Navarre from 1234 as Theobald I. Theobald, h
2 CONC owever, repudiated her before 1223. In 1224, she married her third husband, Simon III of Saarbrücken and Leiningen (d. 1234/36), the son of Count Frederick II of Leiningen and Saarbrücken. When she died childless, her third husban
2 CONC d Simon of Leiningen inherited the county of Dagsburg, thus creating the Leiningen-Dagsburg line.
