1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''OTTO [II] "der Reiche" (-1113) Graaf van Zutphen.''' 
2 CONT s/o GOTTSCHALK  Graaf van Twenthe. Graaf van Zutphen. Graf in der Hetter & ADELHEID van Zutphen
2 CONT x JUDITH, daughter of --- (-[1118])
2 CONT * HENDRIK (-before 1134) Graaf van Zutphen. x MATHILDE von Beichlingen
2 CONT * DIRK (-before 1134) Bishop
2 CONT * GERAARD (-before 1134)
2 CONT * ERMGARD (-after 1134)
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#Gottschalkdied1063
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1.         [GOTTSCHALK (-killed in battle 1063 or 1064).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Graaf van Twenthe 1027.  Graaf van Zutphen 1037-1054.  "Heinricus…Romanorum imperator augustus
2 CONC " donated "Mehgida…in comitatu Godeschalci comitis et in pago Westvalen" to the Stift St Simon und Juda at Goslar by charter dated 27 Mar 1052[1289].  "Godescalci comitis Thuente" is named in a charter of bishop Bernulf dated befo
2 CONC re 1054[1290].  Graf in der Hetter 1062.]  m ADELHEID van Zutphen, daughter of OTTO Graaf van Zutphen & his wife ---.  Heiress of Zutphen and the Vogteien of Münster and Borghorst.  "Comiti Godescalco et uxori suæ Adelhaidæ et eor
2 CONC um filiis Gebehardo et Ottoni" reached agreement with Wilhelm Bishop of Utrecht concerning certain payments, by charter dated 1059[1291].  Graf Gottschalk & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         GEBHARD (-after 1059).  "Comiti Godescalco et uxori suæ Adelhaidæ et eorum filiis Gebehardo et Ottoni" reached agreement with Wilhelm Bishop of Utrecht concerning certain payments, by charter dated 1059[1292]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >b)         OTTO [II] "der Reiche" (-1113).  "Comiti Godescalco et uxori suæ Adelhaidæ et eorum filiis Gebehardo et Ottoni" reached agreement with Wilhelm Bishop of Utrecht concerning certain payments, by charter dated 1059[1293].
2 CONC   Graaf van Zutphen.  Anno Archbishop of Köln divided the church of Neutz St. Qurin, founded by "Euerhardus comes Clivensis et matrona nobilis Berta comitissa uxor sua" between the church and the archbishopric by charter dated 27 
2 CONC Sep 1074, witnessed by "Otto comes de Zutphen et de Gelrie..."[1294].  Burchard Bishop of Utrecht granted privileges to the church of St Peter and St Walburgis in Zutphen, at the request of “comitis domini Ottonis”, by charter dat
2 CONC ed 1105[1295].  Heinrich V King of Germany confirmed donations to the church of Zutphen made by “domini Ottonis comitis de Sutfenne et filii eius Heinrici” by charter dated 28 Dec 1107[1296].  Vogt von Corvey.  The Annales Colonie
2 CONC nses Maximi record the death in 1113 of “Otto...comes de Sudvene”[1297].  m JUDITH, daughter of --- (-[1118]).  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 1134 which records the donation by "Domina Ermengardis comitissa…hæres le
2 CONC gitima oppidi Sutphaniensis…cum marito suo Cunrado comite de Lucelenburg et filio suo Henrico" of "ecclesiam Lochemensem", confirmed by the bishop of Utrecht, for the souls of "mariti sui Gerardi…domini Ottonis comitis patris sui 
2 CONC et matris suæ Judithæ et fratrum suorum piæ memoriæ…episcopi Theodrici et comitum Henrici et Gerardi"[1298].  Graf Otto [II] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>i)          HENDRIK (-before 1134).  His parentage is confirmed by a charter dated 1134 which records the donation by "Domina Ermengardis comitissa…hæres legitima oppidi Sutphaniensis…cum marito suo Cunrado comite de Lucelenburg
2 CONC  et filio suo Henrico" of "ecclesiam Lochemensem", confirmed by the bishop of Utrecht, for the souls of "mariti sui Gerardi…domini Ottonis comitis patris sui et matris suæ Judithæ et fratrum suorum piæ memoriæ…episcopi Theodrici e
2 CONC t comitum Henrici et Gerardi"[1299].  Heinrich V King of Germany confirmed donations to the church of Zutphen made by “domini Ottonis comitis de Sutfenne et filii eius Heinrici” by charter dated 28 Dec 1108[1300].  Graaf van Zutph
2 CONC en.  Heinrich V King of Germany granted "comitatum Frisie" to "comiti Henrico de Zutphenne" in return for "beneficii Alcei" by charter dated 28 Dec 1108[1301].  The Annales Colonienses Maximi record a dispute in 1114 between Fried
2 CONC rich Archbishop of Köln and “ducis de Lovene Godefridi et comitis Westfalie Friderici fratrisque sui Heinrici et Theoderici de Are et Heinrici de Sudvene et Heinrici de Linburg”[1302].  Friedrich [I] Archbishop of Köln divided the
2 CONC  church of Zyfflich by charter dated 1117 witnessed by "Godefridus dux, Fridericus comes de Arnesberg, Arnoldus de Clive, Heinricus comes de Sutuene…"[1303].  m MATHILDE von Beichlingen, daughter of KUNO Graf von Beichlingen & his
2 CONC  wife Kunigunde von Weimar .  The Annalista Saxo records (but does not name, except for the fourth daughter) the four daughters of Kuno & his wife, one of whom (listed first) married "Heinricus comes de Suitfene"[1304].  The prima
2 CONC ry source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  1117. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>ii)         DIRK (-before 1134).  His parentage is confirmed by a charter dated 1134 which records the donation by "Domina Ermengardis comitissa…hæres legitima oppidi Sutphaniensis…cum marito suo Cunrado comite de Lucelenburg et
2 CONC  filio suo Henrico" of "ecclesiam Lochemensem", confirmed by the bishop of Utrecht, for the souls of "mariti sui Gerardi…domini Ottonis comitis patris sui et matris suæ Judithæ et fratrum suorum piæ memoriæ…episcopi Theodrici et c
2 CONC omitum Henrici et Gerardi"[1305].  Bishop. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iii)        GERAARD (-before 1134).  His parentage is confirmed by a charter dated 1134 which records the donation by "Domina Ermengardis comitissa…hæres legitima oppidi Sutphaniensis…cum marito suo Cunrado comite de Lucelenburg
2 CONC  et filio suo Henrico" of "ecclesiam Lochemensem", confirmed by the bishop of Utrecht, for the souls of "mariti sui Gerardi…domini Ottonis comitis patris sui et matris suæ Judithæ et fratrum suorum piæ memoriæ…episcopi Theodrici e
2 CONC t comitum Henrici et Gerardi"[1306]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iv)        ERMGARD (-after 1134).  A charter dated 1134 records the donation by "Domina Ermengardis comitissa…hæres legitima oppidi Sutphaniensis…cum marito suo Cunrado comite de Lucelenburg et filio suo Henrico" of "ecclesiam L
2 CONC ochemensem", confirmed by the bishop of Utrecht, for the souls of "mariti sui Gerardi…domini Ottonis comitis patris sui et matris suæ Judithæ et fratrum suorum piæ memoriæ…episcopi Theodrici et comitum Henrici et Gerardi"[1307].  
2 CONC Heiress of Zütphen.  Neptis of Emperor Lothar [von Süpplingenburg], although the primary source which confirms this, and the precise relationship, has not yet been identified.  m firstly ([1115/17]) GERHARD [II] Graaf van Gelre, s
2 CONC on of GERHARD [I] "Flaminius" Graaf van Wassenberg & his [first wife ---] (-before 1134).  m secondly (before 1134) CONRAD II Comte de Luxembourg, son of GUILLAUME I Comte de Luxembourg & his wife Luitgard von Beichlingen ([1106/1
2 CONC 2?]-after 30 May 1135). 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#Gottschalkdied1063
2 CONT ----
