1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Medilands (''Mar 2022'') [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAR.htm#ThierryIdied1105B Bar: Chapter 2. Comtes de Mousson]====
2 CONT '''THIERRY de Mousson''', son of LOUIS Comte de Mousson & his wife Sophie of Upper Lotharingia ([1045]-1/2 Jan 1103, bur Autun Cathedral). 
2 CONT >The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' names "''Theodericum''" as son of "''comiti Montionis Ludovico''" and his wife Sophie[69].  
2 CONT >"''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis''…" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "''suis antecessoribus…Lodewico, Sophia eius uxore, et filiis eorum Brunone, Theode
2 CONC rico, Lodewico, Friderico, filiabus vero Mathilde, Sophia, Beatrice''…"[70].  
2 CONT >On his marriage, he entered into possession of the château and seigneurie de Montbéliard[71].  
2 CONT >He succeeded his father in [1071/76] in his territories of Altkirch, Ferrette, and around Hagenau.  He was present at the 1076 enfranchisement of the chapel in the castle of Amance[72].  
2 CONT >He inherited the region of the future county of Bar from his mother in 1093.  
2 CONT >He had taken a vow to join the First Crusade but was released from it due to illness.  
2 CONT >He was invested as Comte de Verdun after 1096 by Richer Bishop of Verdun[73].  
2 CONT >He dictated his testament in 1102 at the castle of Altkirch[74].  
2 CONT >The ''Obituaire de Saint-Mansuy-lès-Toul'' records the death "1 Jan" of "''Henricus et Theodoricus comites''"[75].  
2 CONT '''m''' ([1065]) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY%20Kingdom.htm#ErmentrudeBourgognedied1105 '''ERMENTRUDE de Bourgogne'''] heiress of Montbéliard, daughter of GUILLAUME I "l''e Grand''" Comte Palatin de Bourgogne & his wi
2 CONC fe Etiennette --- ([1050/55]-1106 or after, bur Autun Cathedral).  
2 CONT >The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' names "''Ermentrudem''" as wife of "''Theodericum [filius comiti Montionis Ludovico'']" specifying that she was heiress to Montbéliard[76].  
2 CONT >"''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "''suis antecessoribus… Lodewico, S
2 CONC ophia eius uxore, et filiis eorum Brunone, Theoderico, Lodewico, Friderico, filiabus vero Mathilde, Sophia, Beatrice, filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''", witnessed by "''Henricus de
2 CONC  Suarca cum genero suo Gerunch, Gotefridus filius avunculi eiusdem comitis [Friderici]''"[77].  It is assumed from the expression "''suis antecessoribus''" that all those so described were deceased at the date of the foundation.  
2 CONT >She subscribed her son Renaud's act of sale of the fortress of Commercy to the abbé de Saint-Mihiel in 1106[78].  
2 CONT '''Comte Thierry & his wife had ten children:'''
2 CONT # '''FRÉDÉRIC de Mousson''' ([1074/78]-19 Jul [1160], bur Oelenberg).  "''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus"'' founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter d
2 CONC ated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "''suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[79].  The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' names (in order) "''Theodoricum de
2 CONC  Monte Beliardi, Fredericum de Ferretes…et Renaldum Strabum comitem de Barro Ducis''" as the three brothers of Etienne Archbishop of Metz[80].  He succeeded his father in 1103 in his territories of Altkirch and Ferrette.  "''Fride
2 CONC ricus filius comitis Theoderici de Montebiligardis''" donated "''Altichilchensis ecclesie…consecrato in honore sancti Cristofori martyris''" to Cluny by charter dated 3 Jul 1105 "''laudante matre mea Hermentrude''"[81].  - [http:/
2 CONC /fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ALSACE.htm#FredericIMontbeliarddied1160B '''Comtes de Ferrette'''].  
2 CONT # '''RENAUD de Mousson''' ([1075/77]-1149).  "F''ilia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which s
2 CONC he names "''suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[82].  The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' names "''Raynaldum comitem filium Theoderici Barrensis''"[83
2 CONC ].  ''Comte de Bar et de Mousson''. -  '''''see below''','' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAR.htm#RenaudBardied1149B '''Chapter 2. Comtes de Bar'''].   
2 CONT # '''THIERRY de Mousson''' ([1076/78]-[mid-Jan] 1163).  "''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105
2 CONC  in which she names "''suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[84].  The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' names "''Theodericus" as brother of "Raynaldum…co
2 CONC mes Barri et Montionis''" specifying that Thierry was expelled in 1113 and retained only the county of Montbéliard[85].  - [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkmontb.htm#ThierryMontbeliarddied1163B '''Comtes de Montbéliard'''].  
2 CONC
2 CONT # '''LOUIS de Mousson''' ([1077/79]-murdered 1102).  "''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in
2 CONC  which she names "''suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[86].  It seems unlikely that Louis de Mousson could have been born much later than [1077/79] bearing in mi
2 CONC nd his active participation in the First Crusade.  Albert of Aix names "…''Luodewicus de Monzunz…filius comitis Tirrici de Muntbiliarht''…" among those who took part in the siege of Nikaia, dated to mid-1097 from the context[87]. 
2 CONC  William of Tyre names "''Ludovicus de Moncons''" among those present at the capture of Antioch in 1098[88].  Albert of Aix records that "''comes de Oringis Reinboldus, Ludowicus de Monzuns, Lambertus filius Cononis de Monte Acuto
2 CONC ''" commanded one of the corps of men at the capture of Antioch in Jun 1098[89].  He returned to Altkirch before 1102, when he was killed by some of his own servants[90].  The ''Annales Einsidlenses'' record the death in 1102 of "
2 CONC ''Ludovicus comes de Montplicart''" killed by his servants[91].  He was referred to as one of her deceased children in the 8 Mar 1105 document of his mother.   
2 CONT # '''ÉTIENNE de Mousson''' (-Metz 29 Dec 1162, bur Metz Cathedral).  The ''Gesta Alberonis Archiepiscopi'' names "''episcopum Stephanum, fratrem Rainaldi comes de Monzon''"[92].  Destined for the church from an early age, he was b
2 CONC rought up by his maternal uncle Guy Archbishop of Vienne, later Pope Calixtus II[93].  The ''Consecratio Ecclesiæ Senonensis'' names "''Stephani pater comes Theodericus et avunculus domnus Guido Viennensis archiepiscopus, post urb
2 CONC is Romæ papa''" in relation to the consecration of Sens in 1124[94].  '''Archdeacon of Toul'''.  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/Trier.htm#EtienneMetzdied1162 '''Bishop of Metz'''] 1120.  The ''Gesta Episcoporum Mettensium (Conti
2 CONC nuatio)'' records the succession in 1120 of “''tam Burgundionem quam Lothoringorum...genere... domnus Stephanus...Calixti (papæ) ex sorore nepos''”, and adds that he granted territory to “''fratris sui comitis Barrensis aliorumque
2 CONC  cognatorum et amicorum suorum''” specifying “''castrum Terli...castrumque ducis apud Vicum et munitionem inter Vicum et Marsallum in loco palustri sitam simulque castrum comitis de Hoemberc... castrum... Ramberti-villare...castru
2 CONC mque nobile Lucelnburch...castrum Viviers et partem ducis de Lemburc in castro Rucei... castrum...Mirabel et Falconis-montem...Danubrii et Asperi-montis...apud Spinal turrim...Moronis... castrum... Petro-pertusata...castrum Deulew
2 CONC art...turrim apud Tihecurt...et castrum...Walteri-montis''”[95].  Etienne Bishop of Metz declared that “''frater meus Teodericus comes de Montbiliart''” recognised the incorrectness of his claims relating to Gorze Abbey by charter
2 CONC  dated to [1138/63], which names “''cognati nostri Theoderic, Mettensis primicerii''”[96].  Etienne Bishop of Metz donated “''prædium in feodo Commarciensi...Bernaicuria ...sylvam etiam Commarciensem...Foreid” to Riéval “per manum
2 CONC  comitis Rainaldi præfati Commarciensis feodi possessoris... collaudante filiisque eius Hugone et Rainaldo''” by undated charter, witnessed by “''Gerardo castellano''...”[97].  Etienne Bishop of Metz donated “''molendinum in Comma
2 CONC rciensi''” to Riéval abbey “''comite... Renaldo et ab utroque eius filio Ugone et Renaldo, a dominoque Stephano Metensi episcopo''” by charter dated 9 Mar 1141 (O.S.?)[98].  He accompanied his brother Renaud on the Second Crusade 
2 CONC in 1147[99].  The ''Gesta Episcoporum Mettensium (Continuatio)'' records the death “''III Kal Jan''” of "''Stephanus''" and his burial “''iuxta chori''”[100].   
2 CONT # '''GUILLAUME de Mousson''' (-before 8 Mar 1105).  The mid-12th century ''Genealogica ex Stirpe Sancti Arnulfi'' names (in order) "''Rainaldum, Theodericum, Fridericum, Willelmum et Stephanum episcopum Metensem fratres" as sons o
2 CONC f "Theodericus''"[101].  "''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "''suis ant
2 CONC ecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[102].   
2 CONT # '''HUGUES de Mousson''' (-before 8 Mar 1105).  "''Filia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus''" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in whi
2 CONC ch she names "''suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderici atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone''"[103].   
2 CONT # '''GUNTHILDE de Mousson''' (-21 Feb 1131).  Her father founded the abbey of Bibliesheim in 1100 and installed his daughter Gunthilde as first abbess[104].  She was canonised[105].   
2 CONT # '''AGNES de Mousson''' (-after 1140).  The ''Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines'' refers to the sister of "''Theodoricum de Monte Beliardi, Fredericum de Ferretes…et Renaldum Strabum comitem de Barro Ducis''" as the wife of
2 CONC  "''Hermanno de Salmis''", and their sons "H''enricum de Salmis et fratrem eius Theodericum abbatem sancti Pauli Virdunensis''"[106].  A charter dated 1147 confirms the agreement between "''comitissa Agnes et heredes de Languesten
2 CONC ''" and "''Bencelinus de Turquesten cum filio suo Conone''" and others relating to the abbey of Haute-Seille, with the consent of "''comitissam Agnetem de Languesten cum filiis suis Henrico et Hermanno consulibus, Conrardum…comite
2 CONC m cum uxore sua Havyde et filio Hugone''"[107].  She is named in the charter dated 1174 under which "''Henricus comes de Salmis''" confirmed donations to the abbey of Haute-Seille by "''patrui mei comitis Hermani aviæque meæ Agnet
2 CONC is''"[108].  A further detail is added by the charter dated 1186 under which "''Henricus comes de Salmis''" confirmed donations to the abbey of Haute-Seille by "''Agnetem comitissam de Langesten aviam meam, Henricum patrem meum et
2 CONC  Hermanum fratrem eius, consules''"[109].  "''Agnes comitissa''" confirmed donations to the abbey of Saint-Sauveur for the soul of "''comitis Godefridi mariti mei''"[110], "Godefridi" presumably being a copyist's error for "''Herm
2 CONC anni''".  '''m''' ([1104]) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LUXEMBOURG.htm#HermannISalmdied1138 '''HERMANN Graf von Salm'''], son of HERMANN Graf von Salm King of Germany & his wife --- ([1075]-[1135]).   
2 CONT # '''MATHILDE de Mousson'''.  Suger records the marriage of "''Albertus nobilis comes Morspecensis''" and "''filiam Theoderici viri clarissimi de Monte Beliardo''" who brought her husband various possessions of Saint-Denis "Blites
2 CONC torp, Tatingum, Sulces, Fardulviler, Fehingas, Viler, Hoenchirche, Torneswile, Pretene" as dowry[111].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  '''m''' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WURTTEMBERG.
2 CONC htm#AdalbertMorsbergMMathildeMontbeliard '''ADALBERT Graf von Mörsberg'''], son of --- (-before 30 Aug 1125). 
2 CONT
