2 CONT
2 CONT '''FREDERIC''', son of THIERRY de Mousson & his wife Ermentrude de Bourgogne [Comté] ([1074/78]-19 Jul [1160], bur Oelenberg).  He was mentioned first in order in the list of his mother's living children in her 1105 document.  "Fi
2 CONC lia Wilelmi comitis de Burgundia Hermentrudis et filii sui Fridericus, Raginaudus, Theodericus" founded the Cluniac abbey of Froidefontaine by charter dated 8 Mar 1105 in which she names "suis antecessoribus…filiis autem Theoderic
2 CONC i atque sue uxoris Hermentrudis, Lodewico, Wilelmo, Hugone"[304].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names (in order) "Theodoricum de Monte Beliardi, Fredericum de Ferretes…et Renaldum Strabum comitem de Barro Ducis" as 
2 CONC the three brothers of Etienne Archbishop of Metz[305].  During his youth he was miraculously cured of paralysis thanks to Saint Morand[306].  He succeeded his father in 1103 in his territories of Altkirch and Ferrette.  He is titl
2 CONC ed Comte de Montbéliard in his mother's 1105 document.  He subscribed an act in 1111 with his father-in-law[307].  He became avoué of the abbey of Lure on his second marriage[308].  He is titled Comte d'Amance in 1112 and 1137, an
2 CONC d Comte de Ferrette in 1125[309].  "Fridericus comes de Firretho cum uxore mea Stephania et filio meo Lodoyco" founded the monastery of Feldbach by charter dated 1144[310].  The necrology of Basel records the death "XIV Kal Aug" o
2 CONC f "Fridericus comes de Ferreto" and his burial "in Oelenberg"[311].  m firstly (before 12 Apr 1111) '''PETRISSA von Zähringen''', daughter of BERTHOLD Herzog von Zähringen (-[1115]).  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a 
2 CONC charter dated to [1115] which records that "domina Petrissa, filia ducis Bertholdi" donated "predium…apud Volpach", by the hands of "viri sui comitis…Friderici de Phirrith"[312].  m secondly '''ETIENNETTE de Vaudémont''', daughter
2 CONC  of GERARD Comte de Vaudémont [Lorraine] & his wife Heilwig von Egisheim (-[4 Dec 1160/1188], bur Oelenberg).  "Fridericus comes de Firretho cum uxore mea Stephania et filio meo Lodoyco" founded the monastery of Feldbach by charte
2 CONC r dated 1144[313].  The necrology of Basel records the death "II Non Dec" of "Stehania comitissa" and her burial "in Oelenberg"[314].  Comte Frédéric & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT #         LOUIS [I] de Ferrette (-1180).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "comitis Ludovici" as son of "Fredericum de Ferretes"[315].  "Fridericus comes de Firretho cum uxore mea Stephania et filio meo Lodoyco" f
2 CONC ounded the monastery of Feldbach by charter dated 1144[316].  He succeeded his father in [1160] as Comte de Ferrette.  "Ludovicus comes Ferretensis et dominus de Wadens" confirmed donations to the abbey of Rosières by "domini Vual
2 CONC cherii Salinensis et…domini Friderici imperatoris", previous holders of the castle of Vadans {Vadans, canton d´Arbois, Jura}, by charter dated 1173[317].  "Ludvicus comes Ferret, Odo comes de Rupe" are named as present in a charte
2 CONC r dated 6 Sep 1178 which records a judgment by Emperor Friedrich I "Barbarossa" in favour of the abbey of Baume-les-Dames[318].  He was the heir of his maternal uncle Olry de Vaudémont Comte d'Egisheim in 1187[319].  He participat
2 CONC ed in the Third Crusade and was present at the siege of Acre in 1190[320].  m RICHENZA von Habsburg, daughter of WERNER [I] Graf von Habsburg & his wife --- (-Dec 1180).  A Habsburg genealogy names "Adelberctum, Gerdrudem de Mümpe
2 CONC lgard, Richenzam de Fierrito" as the children of "Wernherus"[321].  Louis [I] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT *a)         ULRIC (-murdered 27 Sep 1197).  He succeeded his father in 1180 as Comte de Ferrette.  He was assassinated on the orders of Othon Comte Palatin de Bourgogne[322].  The Annales Maurimonesterienses record that "Hulricus 
2 CONC comes" was killed in 1197[323]. 
2 CONT *b)         LOUIS [II] (-1189).  He succeeded as Comte de Ferrette, Seigneur de Vadans.  He died while on Crusade[324].  m AGNES von Sogren, daughter of UDELARD [II] Graf von Sogren [Soybières/Saugern] & his wife Adelheid ---.  Lo
2 CONC uis & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT **i)          FRIEDRICH [II] (-murdered [1232/25 Jan 1233]).  He succeeded as Comte de Ferrette.    -         see below. 
2 CONT *c)         HELWIDE .  1188.
