1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAR.htm#AgnesMHermannSalm
2 CONT
2 CONT HERMANN [II] von Salm ([1070/75]-[1135]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marries ([1104]) '''AGNES de Mousson''', daughter of THIERRY Comte de Mousson & his wife Ermentrude de Bourgogne [Comté] (-after 1140).
2 CONT
2 CONT *The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the sister of "Theodoricum de Monte Beliardi, Fredericum de Ferretes…et Renaldum Strabum comitem de Barro Ducis" as the wife of "Hermanno de Salmis", and names their sons "Hen
2 CONC ricum de Salmis et fratrem eius Theodericum abbatem sancti Pauli Virdunensis"[237].
2 CONT *A charter dated 1147 confirms the agreement between "comitissa Agnes et heredes de Languesten" and "Bencelinus de Turquesten cum filio suo Conone" and others relating to the abbey of Haute-Seille, with the consent of "comitissam 
2 CONC Agnetem de Languesten cum filiis suis Henrico et Hermanno consulibus, Conrardum…comitem cum uxore sua Havyde et filio Hugone"[238].
2 CONT *She is named in the charter dated 1174 under which "Henricus comes de Salmis" confirmed donations to the abbey of Haute-Seille by "patrui mei comitis Hermani aviæque meæ Agnetis"[239].
2 CONT *A further detail is added by the charter dated 1186 under which "Henricus comes de Salmis" confirmed donations to the abbey of Haute-Seille by "Agnetem comitissam de Langesten aviam meam, Henricum patrem meum et Hermanum fratrem 
2 CONC eius, consules"[240].
2 CONT *"Agnes comitissa" confirmed donations to the abbey of Saint-Sauveur for the soul of "comitis Godefridi mariti mei"[241], "Godefridi" presumably being a copyist's error for "Hermanni".
2 CONT *A charter dated to [1155] or [1160] records the foundation of the abbey of Haute-Seille by “comitissam Agnetem de Languestein cum filiis suis Henrico et Heremanno consulibus, Conrardum...comitem cum uxore sua Havyde et filio Hugo
2 CONC ne”[242].
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Hermann [II] & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # HERMANN [III] von Salm (-after 1147).
2 CONT # HEINRICH [I] von Salm und Langenstein (-after 1153, bur Notre-Dame La Ronde, near Metz Cathedral).
2 CONT # DIETRICH von Salm (-22 Feb 1156).
