2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude of Saxony (also known as Gertrude Billung) (c. 1030 – August 4, 1113), was the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt. She married Floris I, Count of Holland (c. 1017 - June 28, 1061) c. 1050, an
2 CONC d upon his death, her son Dirk V became Count of Holland. Since he was still young, she became regent.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Dirk V came into power, William I, Bishop of Utrecht, took advantage of the situation, occupying territory that he had claimed in Holland. Gertrude and her son withdrew to the islands of Frisia (Zeeland), leaving William to o
2 CONC ccupy the disputed lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian), the second son of Baldwin V of Flanders. This act gave Dirk the Imperial Flanders as an appanage - including the islands of Frisia west of the Frisian Scheldt. She 
2 CONC and her husband then acted as co-regents for the young count.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a total of seven children with Floris I:
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liege. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17 June 1091). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha (ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Machteld (b. ca. 1057) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guînes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From her second marriage to Robert I she had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II of Flanders (c. 1065 – October 5, 1111). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela (d.1115), who first married king Canute IV of Denmark, and was the mother of Charles the Good, later count of Flanders. She then married Roger Borsa, duke of Apulia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude, who married Thierry II, Duke of Lorraine, and was the mother of Thierry of Alsace, also later count of Flanders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Loo, whose illegitimate son William of Ypres was also a claimant to the county of Flanders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogiva, abbess of Messines. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude of Saxony (also known as Gertrude Billung) (c. 1030 – August 4, 1113), was the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt. She married Floris I, Count of Holland (c. 1017 - June 28, 1061) c. 1050, an
2 CONC d upon his death, her son Dirk V became Count of Holland. Since he was still young, she became regent.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Dirk V came into power, William I, Bishop of Utrecht, took advantage of the situation, occupying territory that he had claimed in Holland. Gertrude and her son withdrew to the islands of Frisia (Zeeland), leaving William to o
2 CONC ccupy the disputed lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian), the second son of Baldwin V of Flanders. This act gave Dirk the Imperial Flanders as an appanage - including the islands of Frisia west of the Frisian Scheldt. She 
2 CONC and her husband then acted as co-regents for the young count.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a total of seven children with Floris I:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Albrecht (b. ca. 1051), a canon in Liege.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Dirk V (ca. 1052, Vlaardingen–17 June 1091).
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Pieter (b. ca. 1053), a canon in Liége.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Bertha (ca. 1055–1094, Montreuil-sur-Mer), who married Philip I of France in 1072.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Floris (b. ca. 1055), a canon in Liége.
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. Machteld (b. ca. 1057)
2 CONT
2 CONT    7. Adela (b. ca. 1061), who married Count Baudouin I of Guînes.
2 CONT
2 CONT From her second marriage to Robert I she had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Robert II of Flanders (c. 1065 – October 5, 1111).
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Adela (d.1115), who first married king Canute IV of Denmark, and was the mother of Charles the Good, later count of Flanders. She then married Roger Borsa, duke of Apulia.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Gertrude, who married Thierry II, Duke of Lorraine, and was the mother of Thierry of Alsace, also later count of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Philip of Loo, whose illegitimate son William of Ypres was also a claimant to the county of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Ogiva, abbess of Messines.
