2 CONT
2 CONT   THIERRY de Lorraine, .. ... .... 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly '''SUANHILDE''', daughter of --- (-4 Sep 1132).  "Suavehildis" is named "uxor enim Theoderici comitis" in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin, which records her death and specifies "pro qua ex cognatione consanguinitatis idem
2 CONC  erat occulte" without giving further details of the family relationship[389].  The Flandria Generosa names "comitissa etiam Suanildis", when recording her death and the bad luck which resulted from her consanguinity with her husb
2 CONC and[390].  No details are known about her parentage so speculation about the precise nature of the family relationship between husband and wife is pointless.  "Theoderici…comitis Flandrie…cum generosa uxore mea Suanehilda" confirm
2 CONC ed the privileges and possessions of the abbey of Saint-Pierre de Loo by charter dated 1130, subscribed by "Willelmo filio Philippi comitis"[391]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Count Thierry I & his first wife had one child:
2 CONT
