1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heinrich IV, Graf von Salm
2 CONT Birth: 1222 correct (aged 18 when son was born)
2 CONT Death:  
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIAN%20(LOWER)%20NOBILITY.htm#HeinrichIVSalmdied1292
2 CONT
2 CONT HEINRICH [IV] von Salm, son of HEINRICH von Salm & his wife Marguerite de Bar (-8 Jan 1292 or 8 Jun 1293).  
2 CONT *The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT *Richer records that in 1251 "dominum Henricum…de Salmis" was summoned before the court of the Bishop of Metz for the damage he had done to the church of Senone[297].  
2 CONT *He succeeded his grandfather as Graf von Salm.  
2 CONT *Graf von Bliescastel 1275.  
2 CONT *A charter dated 19 May 1284 records an agreement between the bishop of Metz and "Henri cuens de Salmes, Henris, Jehan et Ferris fill edit conte de Salmes" relating to "la contei de Caistres"[298]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1242 before 12 Feb) as her second husband, 
2 CONT
2 CONT LAURETTE von Bliescastel, widow of --- von Rappoltstein, daughter of HEINRICH Graf von Bliescastel & his wife --- (-Sep 1269).  
2 CONT *The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT *Heiress of Hunolstein, Bernkastel and Püttlingen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich [IV] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT # HEINRICH von Salm (-[14 May/4 Aug] 1288). 
2 CONT # JOHANN [I] von Salm (-after 1330). 
2 CONT # KATHARINA [Johanna] von Salm (-after 1314). 
