1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There is no verification about her parents, sources have only the name Oda, nothing about her origin.
2 CONT
2 CONT erwähnt wurde nur, dass sie aus dem unteren Maasgebiet stammte, die von Rethel lebten in einem ganz anderen Gebiet.= it was only mentioned that she came from the lower Maas region, who lived by Rethel in a very different area.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIA.htm#Godefroidied1069B<br/>
2 CONT GODEFROI, son of GOZELON I Duke of Lower Lotharingia and Upper Lotharingia & his wife --- ([1000/1020]-Verdun 30 Dec 1069, bur Verdun Cathedral).  .. ... ....
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly''' DODA [Guota/Uoda]''', daughter of --- (bur Münsterbilsen).  The Vita B. Idæ Boloniensis Comitissæ records that Ida was the daughter of "pater…Godefridus, mater…Doda"[271].  "Heinricus…rex" confirmed the foundati
2 CONC on and possessions of the convent of Maria Magdalena at Verdun by charter dated 16 Jun 1040, on the petition of "Ricardi Virdunensis ecclesiæ presulis,…quodam suæ dioceseos clerico Ermenfrido, …tempore patris sui Heizelini comitis
2 CONC " which records donations by "…Guota per manus mariti sui Gotefridi ducis…"[272].  The origin of Doda is not known.  Murray suggests[273] that she was the daughter of Manassès [I] Comte de Rethel, her name resembling the name of M
2 CONC anassès's wife.  This proposed origin is presumably inconsistent with Doda's daughter having been the wife of Manassès [II] Comte de Rethel (see below), as the couple would have been first cousins.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT a ''''wiki draft '''' of https://www.geni.com/people/Manass%C3%A8s-II-count-of-Rethel/6000000009958689931 
2 CONT says''[2]'' she  could be https://www.geni.com/people/Doda-de-Rethel/6000000002188307451  his ''(Medlands unknown)'' daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
