1 NAME Berthold II /von Vohburg/
2 GIVN Berthold II
2 _MARNM von Vohburg
1 NAME Berthold II, markgraf von Vohburg
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 MAY 1204
1 OCCU etzter Markgraf von Cham
1 TITL markgraf
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#DiepoldVIIVohburgdied1225
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         BERTHOLD [II] (-25 May 1204).  A charter dated to [1193] (should be dated to before 1185), incorporated in a vidimus dated 1402, records that “Tiemo” donated property to Reichenbach in the presence of "Pertholdi marchio
2 CONC nis" and “per manus Pertholdi patris sui marchionis”[143].  Markgraf von Vohburg 1189.  The Ignoti Monachi Chronica records that the emperor sent "comes Britoldus" to the kingdom of Sicily in 1192 and that he obtained "comitatum M
2 CONC olisii" and destroyed "plures terras cum Corrado marchione"[144].  The Annales Scheftarienses Maiores record that "marchio Voburgensis" died in 1204[145].  Wegener quotes the Chronicon Reichenbach which records the death of "Perht
2 CONC oldus filius Diepoldi marchionis…VIII Kal Jun" without heirs, recording that his Mark was inherited by "Ludovici ducis Bavariæ" whose sister he had married[146].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ELISABETH von Wittelsbach, daughter of OTTO I Duke of Bavaria [Wittelsbach] & his wife Agnes van Looz (-Kloster Biburg [1189/90]).  Wegener quotes the Chronicon Reichenbach which records the death of "Perhtoldus fi
2 CONC lius Diepoldi marchionis…VIII Kal Jun" without heirs, recording that his Mark was inherited by "Ludovici ducis Bavariæ" whose sister he had married[147].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1193) as her second husband, ---, widow of ROBERTO Conte di Caserta, sister of BERARDO, daughter of ---.  The Annales Casenses record the marriage in 1193 of "Bertoldus" and "sororem comitis Berardi relictam comi
2 CONC tis Roberti di Caserta"[148]. 
