2 CONT 2.         BEATRIX (-Wadderoth 17 Jun 1102).  The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Eilica, Iudhita, Beatrix, Gisla, Berta" as the five daughters of Otto von Schweinfurt and Immula, referring to Beatrix's husband as "marchioni" wit
2 CONC hout naming him[1116].  Heiress of Schweinfurt.  The Gesta Archiepiscoporum Magdeburgensium records the death "1102 XV Kal Iul" at "Wadderoth" of "Beatrice, filia Ottonis ducis Suevorum"[1117].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' HEINRICH Graf von Hildrizhausen, son of --- (-1078).  He became Markgraf auf dem Nordgau after the death of his father-in-law.  1054/89.  "Heinricus…rex" granted property "in comitatu Heinrici comitis in pago Nordgove et i
2 CONC n marchia Napvrg" to "nostro servineti Otnant" by charter dated 13 Feb 1061[1118].  "Heinricus…rex" granted property "in pago Nortgowe comitatu vero Heinrici" to the church of Bamberg by charter dated 27 Oct 1069[1119].  The Berno
2 CONC ldi Chronicon records the death in 1078 of "Heinricus marchio"[1120].  
2 CONT
