2 CONT 4.         ALBERADA BERTHA (-11 Jan [1103]).  The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Eilica, Iudhita, Beatrix, Gisla, Berta" as the five daughters of Otto von Schweinfurt and Immula, referring to Berta's husband as "quidam de princi
2 CONC pus Bawariorum, qui agnominatus fuit de municione sua Havekesberh dicta"[1130].  The Fundatio Monasterii Banzensis names "marchio Hermannus…uxorem Alberadam" as founders of the monastery of Banz in [1071], and their two children "
2 CONC Heinricum, Ottonem"[1131].  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
