2 CONT xxx [https://www.geni.com/people/Berthold-I-Graf-von-Schwarzenburg/6000000002187796542?through=6000000009726846426 BERTHOLD] [I] [von Schwarzenberg], son of --- [von Schwarzenberg] & his first wife [Hedwig ---] ([before 1070]-befo
2 CONC re [1108]).]  A charter dated to [1104/08] records donations to Oberaltaich by "Domna Richgard uxor Pertholdi" for the soul of her husband, witnessed by "Adalpreht Comes, Engelpreht filius eius…"[2020].  Wegener speculates that sh
2 CONC e was Richgard von Sponheim, daughter of Engelbert [I] Graf von Sponheim Graf im Pustergau & his wife Hedwig ---, and that Berthold [I] was her first husband before she married Poppo II Marchese di Carniola e Istria and later Gebh
2 CONC ard [I] von Wasserburg[2021].  The chronology of Richgard herself and of her first and second husbands suggests that she could only have married Berthold as her third husband.  This suggestion fits neatly into the present proposed
2 CONC  new reconstruction of the Schwarzenberg/Regensburg family.  One difficulty is that Richgard would have had sons named Engelbert by both her second and third husbands, which seems unlikely.  Berthold [I] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Engelbert-von-Schwarzenberg-Sponheim/6000000009726846426 ENGELBERT] [von Schwarzenberg] ([1102/05]->1125).'''  A''' charter dated to [1104/08] records donations made to Oberaltaich by "Domna Richga
2 CONC rd uxor Pertholdi" for the soul of her husband, witnessed by "Adalpreht Comes, Engelpreht filius eius…"[2022].  1125.  x NN  The primary source which confirms the family origin of Engelbert’s wife has not been identified.  Engelbe
2 CONC rt & his wife had [one child]:''' 
2 CONT >>(a)       [https://www.geni.com/people/Berthold-von-Schwarzenburg-II/6000000016821575847?through=6000000009726846426 BERTHOLD] [II] von Schwarzenberg ([1125]-on crusade 23 Aug [1148]).  A charter dated 12 Feb 1150 records that “
2 CONC Berchtoldo de Swarcenburc in expeditione Ierosolimitana morte prævento” had donated “prædium Doberseze”, which “domini Friderici Coloniensis archiepiscopi patrui sui” had given him, to Bamberg St Michael[2023].  The primary source
2 CONC  which confirms that Berthold [II] was the son of Engelbert has not been identified, although his date of death suggests that he belonged to the generation immediately succeeding Engelbert’s generation and the reference to “Schwar
2 CONC zenberg” links him to Engelbert’s family.] 
2 CONT
