1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elżbieta wrocławska''' (ur. w latach 1224-1232[1], zm. 16 stycznia 1265 w Modrzu) – '''śląska księżniczka''', '''księżna wielkopolska''', córka Henryka II Pobożnego. http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/El%C5%BCbieta_wr
2 CONC oc%C5%82awska
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth of Wrocław also known as Elisabeth of Poland (polish: Elżbieta wrocławska ca. 1232 – 16 January 1265) was a daughter of Henry II the Pious and his wife Anna of Bohemia . She was a member of the House of Piast  and was Du
2 CONC chess of Greater Poland  by her marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth spent her childhood in Sanctuary of St. Jadwiga in Trzebnica were she would have lived with her paternal grandmother Hedwig, who would have been a big influence to her granddaughter. It is not certain whether there was p
2 CONC ressure for Elisabeth to join the monastry. Elisabeth remained at Trzebnica until she was kidnapped by her brother Boleslaw II the Bald  because her family wanted her to marry Przemysl I of Greater Poland .
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage was for political reasons like most royal marriages of the time. Przemysł wanted to regain some of his father's lost lands in Silesia . The marriage helped the reincorporation of Kalisz  into Greater Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is know of the rule of Elisabeth as Duchess consort of her husband's lands. In 1250 she founded a monastry in Owińska. Some nuns were brought to it from her childhood home of Trzebnica.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth and Przemysł had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Przemysl II , King of Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance (1245/6–1281), married 1260 to Conrad, Margrave of Brandenburg-Stendal . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eufrozyna, Abbess of St. Clara in Trzebnica . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna (1253–after 26 June, 1295 ), Abbess at Owinska . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eufemia (1253–1298), a nun at St. Clara, Wroclaw . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth's husband died June 4, 1257 he left Elisabeth her Oprawa wdowia  in which was an estate in Modrze . Elisabeth died on her estate 16 January 1265.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth's granddaughter from her son was Elisabeth Richeza of Poland  who became the second wife of Wenceslaus II of Bohemia
