2 CONT 3.         '''KINGA [Kunigunde] (1224-24 Jul 1292)'''.  The Annales Cracovienses Compilati records the birth in 1234 of "Kinga filia Bolezlay"[929], the Annales Polonorum clarifying that she was "Kinga fila regis Ungarie Bele et d
2 CONC e matre Maria" born "in dominica quinquagesima"[930].  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record the marriage in 1239 of "Blezlaus filius Lezstkonis" and "filiam regis Hungarie"[931].  Her name is confirmed by the Annales Cracovien
2 CONC ses Compilati which record that "dux Boleslaus accepit Kingam" in 1238[932].  "Bolezlaus filius Lesconis…Dux Cracoviæ et Sandomiriæ" founded the monastery of Krzyzanowice, at the request of "matris nostræ Grzymislavæ", for the sou
2 CONC ls of "patris nostri Lesconis et uxoris nostræ Gunebundis", by charter dated 28 Jun 1254[933].  "Bolezlaus…Cracouie et Sandomirie dux" conferred privileges on the church of Krakow, for the soul of "patris nostri clare memorie Crac
2 CONC ouie et Sandomirie ducis Leztconis" and for "nostre genitricis ducisse Grimizlaue et…consortis nostre Cungundis", by charter dated 18 May 1255[934].  The Annales Cracovienses Compilati record the deaths in 1279 of "Boleslaus dux m
2 CONC aioris Polonie, Boleslaus dux Cracowie"[935].  She became a nun in 1270.  The Annales Polonorum record the death in 1292 of "domina Kinga ducissa" at Krakow[936].  She was beatified 10 Jun 1690.  m (1239) BOLESŁAV of Poland, son o
2 CONC f LESZKO I "Bialy/the White" Prince of Sandomir and Krakow & his wife Gremislava Ingvarevna of Luck and Dorogobuz [Rurikid] (21 Jun 1226-7 Dec 1279).  He succeeded in 1243 as BOLESŁAW V "Wstydliwy/the Modest" Prince of Krakow and 
2 CONC Sandomir. 
2 CONT *Her parents: BÉLA, son of ANDRÁS II King of Hungary & his first wife Gertrud von Andechs-Merano (Nov 1206-Margaret Island, near Buda 2/3 May 1270, bur Esztergom). BÉLA IV King of Hungary and ...m (1218) MARIA Laskarina, daughter 
2 CONC of THEODOROS Laskaris Emperor in Nikaia & his first wife Anna Angelina (-16 or 24 Jul 1270, bur Esztergom). 
2 CONT *Her siblings:
2 CONT **1.         KATHARINA (-Klis Castle 1242, bur Split St Domnius). 
2 CONT **2.         MARGIT "the Elder" (-Klis Castle 20 Apr 1242, bur Split St Dominius). 
2 CONT **3.         ''KINGA [Kunigunde] (1224-24 Jul 1292).''  '''Herself'''
2 CONT **4.         ANNA [Agnes] ([1226/27]-). ... m (1243) ROSTISLAV Mikhailovich ex-Prince of Galich, son of MIKHAIL Vsevolodich Grand Prince of Kiev & his wife Maria Romanovna of Galich ([1225]-1263).  
2 CONT **5.         ELISABETH (1236-24 Oct 1271, bur Kloster Seligenthal). ... m (1250) HEINRICH von Bayern, son of OTTO II "der Erlauchte" Duke of Bavaria & his wife Agnes von Sachsen [Este] (Landshut 19 Nov 1235-Burghausen 3 Feb 1290, 
2 CONC bur Kloster Seligenthal). 
2 CONT **6.         KONSTANZA.  Baumgarten names the wife of Prince Lev and gives her origin citing sources in support[956].  m ([1251/52]) LEV Daniilovich of Galich, son of DANIIL Romanovich Grand Prince of Kiev, King of Galich & his fi
2 CONC rst wife Anna Mstislavna of Novgorod ([1228]-1301). 
2 CONT **7.         ISTVÁN (Dec 1239-1 Aug 1272).  ... He succeeded his father in 1270 as ISTVÁN V King of Hungary. 
2 CONT **8.         MARGIT "the Younger" (1242-18 Jan 1271). ... m (1250) BOLESŁAW of Poland, son of WŁADYSŁAW Prince of Greater Poland & his wife Hedwig [von Pommerellen] (after 1221-13 Apr 1279).
2 CONT **9.         IOLANDA [Helena] ([1238/44]-16/17 Jun after 1303).  ... m (1250) BOLESŁAW of Poland, son of WŁADYSŁAW Prince of Greater Poland & his wife Hedwig [von Pommerellen] (after 1221-13 Apr 1279). 
2 CONT **10.      BÉLA ([1245]-1269, bur Gran [Esztergom]). ... m (24/25 Oct 1264) as her first husband, KUNIGUNDE von Brandenburg, daughter of OTTO III Markgraf von Brandenburg [Askanier] & his wife Beatrix [Božena] of Bohemia ([1247/52
2 CONC ]-after 8 Jun 1292). 
2 CONT
