1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Euphemia von Rieneck1,2
2 CONT Last Edited	21 Dec 1998
2 CONT '''F, #67314, d. after 1299'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Ludwig II, Graf von Rieneck, Burggraf von Mainz, Stifter von Himmelthal1,2 d. 9 May 1243
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Adelheid von Henneberg1,2 d. a 1253
2 CONT '''Euphemia von Rieneck married Boppo I von Durn, Graf von Dilsberg''', son of Konrad von Durn and Mechtild von Laufen, '''before 9 May 1253.1,2 Euphemia von Rieneck died after 1299.'''1,2
2 CONT '''Family	Boppo I von Durn, Graf von Dilsberg''' d. bt 25 Jul 1276 - 22 Nov 1276
2 CONT '''Child'''	
2 CONT *Boppo II von Durn, Graf von Dilsberg+1,2 d. bt 23 Jan 1290 - 12 May 1290
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1. [S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. XVI, Tafel 154a.
2 CONT 2. [S11582] CD-ROM: Nobility of the Holy Roman Empire and Other European Nobility, by GenQuest.
2 CONT From: https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2241.htm#i67314
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT Chapter 19.  GRAFEN von RIENECK
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT 6.         '''[EUPHEMIA von Rieneck (-after 26 Jun 1280).  The primary source which confirms her precise parentage has not been identified.  From a chronological point of view, it is likely that she was the daughter''' of Ludwig [
2 CONC II] Graf von Rieneck. ''' “Evfemia de Rienecke, dni Bopponis de Durne relicta” donated property "in Adolfesehim...Sucigeris hof" to Seligenthal, with the consent of “meorum filiorum Bopponis et Ludewici”, by charter dated 22 Nov 1
2 CONC 276[1475].  “Eufemia relicta...Bopponis quondam comitis de Durne, Boppo et Ludewicus filii mei” granted rights to Amorbach by charter dated 26 Jun 1280[1476].  m POPPO [I] Herr von Dürn''', son of KONRAD [I] Herr von Dürn & his wi
2 CONC fe Mechtild von Laufen '''(-before 1273).  Graf von Dilsberg.''' 
2 CONT From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA.htm#EuphemiaRieneckMPoppoDurn
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapter 12.  HERREN von DÜRN
2 CONT KONRAD [I] von Dürn (-17 Sep 1258).  “Cunradus de Durne” acquired "advocaciam in Slierstat", with the consent of “uxoris nostre Mehthildis et filii nostri Bopponis nec non aliorum liberorum nostrorum Ruperti et Ulrici”, with the a
2 CONC greement of Kloster Seligenthal, by charter dated 13 Oct 1248[909].  “Cunradus de Durna advocatus ecclesie in Amorbach et conjux Mechtildis filia comitis de Loufe communicata manu filiorum nostrorum Bopponis, Ruperti et Odalrici” 
2 CONC donated property to Kloster Amorbach by charter dated 1253[910].  He was named as deceased in the 1258 charter witnessed by his widow, quoted below.  m MECHTILD von Laufen, daughter of POPPO [V] Graf von Laufen & his wife Adelheid
2 CONC  von Vohburg (-[25 Jul 1276/Jan 1277]).  "Conrado de Durne et Mechtilde nata com. de Lauff." founded Kloster Seligenthal by charter dated 1236[911].  "Cunradus de Durne et uxor sua Methildis matrona nobilis" donated property “in v
2 CONC illa Slirstat” to Würzburg for Seligenthal by charter dated 1239[912].  “Cunradus de Durne” acquired "advocaciam in Slierstat", with the consent of “uxoris nostre Mehthildis et filii nostri Bopponis nec non aliorum liberorum nostr
2 CONC orum Ruperti et Ulrici”, with the agreement of Kloster Seligenthal, by charter dated 13 Oct 1248[913].  “Cunradus de Durna advocatus ecclesie in Amorbach et conjux Mechtildis filia comitis de Loufe communicata manu filiorum nostro
2 CONC rum Bopponis, Ruperti et Odalrici” donated property to Kloster Amorbach by charter dated 1253[914].  “Boppo et Rupertus fratres de Durne, Mehthildis mater eorumdem [...relicte de Durne], Mehthildis de Brunekke, Mehthildis de Scowe
2 CONC nberc...” witnessed the charter dated 1258 which records that Seligenthal bought "silvam...Vrfaze"[915].  “Luckardis comitissa de Zygenhagen” donated property “in Heimesbach” to Kloster Seligenthal, with the consent of “matris suæ
2 CONC  Methildis comitissæ de Durne et fratrum suorum Bopponis et Ruperti”, by charter dated 24 Jul 1267, witnessed by “Boppo comes de Tyeligisberc, Rupertus de Durne, Engelhardus de Berlichingen”[916].  “Methildis comitissa de Durne, R
2 CONC upertus et Ulrici filii nostri” confirmed that "matrona dicta Dingele..." had donated property “in Ruchsheim” to Seligenthal by charter dated 29 Mar 1270[917].  “Methildis domina de Durne” donated property to Seligenthal by charte
2 CONC r dated 10 Nov 1274[918].  “Methildis...comitissa de Durne” confirmed the donation to Seligenthal made by “Otto miles dictus Hornasse...” by charter dated 25 Jul 1276[919].  She was named as deceased in the [3] Feb 1277 charter of
2 CONC  her sons.  Konrad [I] & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT *a)         '''POPPO [I] von Dürn''' (-before 1273).  “Cunradus de Durne” acquired "advocaciam in Slierstat", with the consent of “uxoris nostre Mehthildis et filii nostri Bopponis nec non aliorum liberorum nostrorum Ruperti et Ul
2 CONC rici”, with the agreement of Kloster Seligenthal, by charter dated 13 Oct 1248[920].  “Cunradus de Durna advocatus ecclesie in Amorbach et conjux Mechtildis filia comitis de Loufe communicata manu filiorum nostrorum Bopponis, Rupe
2 CONC rti et Odalrici” donated property to Kloster Amorbach by charter dated 1253[921].  Herr von Dürn.  “Boppo et Rupertus fratres de Durne, Mehthildis mater eorumdem [...relicte de Durne], Mehthildis de Brunekke, Mehthildis de Scowenb
2 CONC erc...” witnessed the charter dated 1258 which records that Seligenthal bought "silvam...Vrfaze"[922].  Graf von Dilsberg: “Poppo de Durn comes de Dilnsperg” acknowledged receiving payments from Ludwig II Duke of Bavaria by charte
2 CONC r dated 4 Nov 1262[923].  “Luckardis comitissa de Zygenhagen” donated property “in Heimesbach” to Kloster Seligenthal, with the consent of “matris suæ Methildis comitissæ de Durne et fratrum suorum Bopponis et Ruperti”, by charter
2 CONC  dated 24 Jul 1267, witnessed by “Boppo comes de Tyeligisberc, Rupertus de Durne, Engelhardus de Berlichingen”[924].  '''m EUPHEMIA von Rieneck, daughter''' of [LUDWIG [II] Graf von Rieneck & his wife Adelheid von Henneberg] '''(-
2 CONC after 22 Nov 1276).  The primary source which confirms her precise parentage has not been identified.  From a chronological point of view, it is likely that she was the daughter of Ludwig [II] Graf von Rieneck.  “Evfemia de Rienec
2 CONC ke, dni Bopponis de Durne relicta” donated property "in Adolfesehim...Sucigeris hof" to Seligenthal, with the consent of “meorum filiorum Bopponis et Ludewici”, by charter dated 22 Nov 1276[925].  “Eufemia relicta...Bopponis quond
2 CONC am comitis de Durne, Boppo et Ludewicus filii mei” granted rights to Amorbach by charter dated 26 Jun 1280[926].  Poppo [I] & his wife had two children''': 
2 CONT **i)          POPPO [II] von Dürn (-after 1290).  “Boppo de Durne” recorded the testament of "bone mem. Boppone genitore nostro" by charter dated 1273, sealed by “Bopponis comitis de Tiligisberc”[927].  “Rupertus et Ulricus fratre
2 CONC s et Boppo fratruelis eorum nobiles de Durne” confirmed donations made to Seligenthal by “felicis memorie mater nostra Mehtildis” by charter dated [3] Feb 1277[928].  “Eufemia relicta...Bopponis quondam comitis de Durne, Boppo et 
2 CONC Ludewicus filii mei” granted rights to Amorbach by charter dated 26 Jun 1280[929].  “Boppo comes de Durne” sold “duas vineas...iuxta Ruchesheim” to Seligenthal, with the consent of “coniugis mee Agnetis de Hohinloch, fratris mei L
2 CONC udewici”, by charter dated early Apr 1282[930].  “Poppo et Ludewicus fratres de Durna” confirmed the sale of property to Amorbach made by “Mechtildis...quondam ava nostra” by charter dated 1290[931].  m AGNES von Hohenlohe, daught
2 CONC er of GOTTFRIED von Hohenlohe Conte di Romagna & his wife Richeza [von Bochsberg] (-after Apr 1282).  "Jutta von Schillingsfürst" donated property to Kloster Schäftersheim, naming "materteræ meæ dominæ Richzæ de Hohenloe et suorum
2 CONC  filiorum meorum consanguineorum Alberti…Craftonis et Cunradi" as guarantors for her wishes to be executed, by charter dated 10 Dec 1262, witnessed by "domina Richza de Hohenloe, Albertus, Crafto, Cunradus filii eius, Agnes filia 
2 CONC eius, Willebirck de Wertheim, Godefridus filius Alberti de Hohenloe…"[932].  “Boppo comes de Durne” sold “duas vineas...iuxta Ruchesheim” to Seligenthal, with the consent of “coniugis mee Agnetis de Hohinloch, fratris mei Ludewici
2 CONC ”, by charter dated early Apr 1282[933].  Poppo [II] & his wife had two children 
2 CONT ***(1)       ALBRECHT von Dürn .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified. 
2 CONT ***(2)       MECHTILD von Dürn ).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified. m FRIEDRICH [II] Schenk von Limpurg, son of --- (-1317). 
2 CONT **ii)         LUDWIG von Dürn (-25 Oct 1295).  “Eufemia relicta...Bopponis quondam comitis de Durne, Boppo et Ludewicus filii mei” granted rights to Amorbach by charter dated 26 Jun 1280[934].  “Boppo comes de Durne” sold “duas vi
2 CONC neas...iuxta Ruchesheim” to Seligenthal, with the consent of “coniugis mee Agnetis de Hohinloch, fratris mei Ludewici”, by charter dated early Apr 1282[935].  “Poppo et Ludewicus fratres de Durna” confirmed the sale of property to
2 CONC  Amorbach made by “Mechtildis...quondam ava nostra” by charter dated 1290[936].  “Graf Ludwig von Dürn” granted “die Hälfte der Stadt Buchen...” to “Konrad von Weinsberg dem Älteren und Konrad dem Jüngeren” by charter dated 25 Oct
2 CONC  1295[937]. 
