1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =HEINRICH II von Stolberg=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Heinrich II de Rijke von Nassau, Count von Nassau and Mechtild (Mathilda) van Gelre en Zutphen 
2 CONT * Heinrich II von Stolberg ( German : Heinrich II von Stolberg ; * c. 1210 in Voigstadt ; † c. 20 May 1272 ) of the Stolberg family was Count and master of Stolberg .
2 CONT * Dynasty: Shcholberg
2 CONT * Heinrich II von Stolberg ( German : Heinrich II von Stolberg ; * c. 1210 in Voigstadt ; † c. 20 May 1272 ) of the Stolberg family was Count and master of Stolberg.
2 CONT * He was the son of Count Heinrich I von Stolberg- Voigschett († d. June 12, 1239), who in 1210 became Count of Stolberg. He was the brother of Count Friedrich von Stolberg-Foxtedt († 1282), Christian († c. 1284), canon of Halbers
2 CONC tadt (1241), Mainz (1259), Würzburg (1267 - 1272), etc., and of Conrad, canon of Würzburg (1257 - 1272).
2 CONT * Henry, Dynasty: Shcholberg (died 28 May after 1247),[1] was a monk in Arnstein Abbey.  HEINRICH (-28 May). "Heinricus comes de Nassowe et Mectildis comitissa" donated "ecclesiam in Inferi[ori] Diffenbach" to Kloster Arnstein by 
2 CONC charter dated 1247, witnessed by "…filiorum nostrorum Walerami, Ottonis, Henrici, Gerardi, Johannis"[82]. Monk at Arnstein. 1247.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Heinrich II married in 1234 to '''Adelheid von Henneberg''' († c. 1259), widow of Count Ludwig II von Rineck († 1243), daughter of Count Popo VII von Henneberg , burgrave of Würzburg († 1245) and Elizabeth von Wildberg († 1220).
2 CONC  Heinrich II, Graf & Herr von Stolberg married Jutta von Hadmersleben, daughter of Bodo von Hadmersleben and Irmgard von Beichlingen, after 29 July 1306 at of Stolberg, Sachsen, Prussia.1,2 Heinrich III, Graf & Herr von Stolberg d
2 CONC ied between 22 August 1329 and 29 August.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Heinrich III von Stolberg''' († 1329/1331/1347), Count and Lord of Stolberg, married ca. 1270 for Utah († 1303/1306), II. July 29, 1306 in Stolberg for '''Jutta von Hadmersleben''' († Fig. 1347)
2 CONT * '''Heinrich''' († 29 January 1357), domcher in Merseburg (1319), domcher in Würzburg (1319 - 1340), domcher in Magdeburg and Kamin (1326), provost in Mozbach (1331), bishop of Merseburg (1341 - 1357)
2 CONT * '''Friedrich von Stolberg the Elder''' († 1314), domcher in Würzburg (1267 - 1313), archdeacon and anti-bishop of Würzburg (1313 - 1314)
2 CONT * '''Heinrich the Elder''' († d. October 21, 1327), domcher in Würzburg (1290 - 1312), archdeacon in Würzburg (1318), cathedral scholasticus in Merseburg (1320 - 1324), probably from the second marriage Dietrich († pp. 1306), cano
2 CONC n of Würzburg
2 CONT * '''Dietrich''' († pp. 1306), canon of Würzburg
2 CONT * '''Elger''' († c. 1316), canon of Würzburg, in a sacred order
2 CONT * '''Heinrich the Younger''' (d. 1340), domcher in Würzburg (1306 - 1340), domcher in Merseburg (1313 - 1329), archdeacon in Würzburg (1318)
2 CONT * '''Heinrich''' († 11 February 1342/24 August 1344), domcher of Würzburg (1319), cathedral prior of Magdeburg (1324 - 1342), elector of Magdeburg (1327)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/THURINGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc512066384 Project MedLands Thuringian Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HEINRICH [II] von Stolberg (-after 20 May 1272).'''  The early 16th century Pauli Iovii Chronicon Schvarzburgicum (which is riddled with errors) records that “...Graff Heinrich und Graff Friedrich Gebrüdere von Stolberg...” wit
2 CONC nessed the charter dated 14 Jul 1242 under which Dietrich Graf von Honstein donated property in the county of Stolberg to Kloster Frankenhausen, with the consent of “seiner Schwester Frauen Bertraten Gräffin zu Beltziz, Frauen Hed
2 CONC wigen seiner Gemahlin und seines altesten Sohnes Graffen Heinrichs”[977].  “...Henricus et Fridericus fratres et comites de Stalberg...” witnessed the charter dated 1249 under which “Henricus et Burchardus de Suarceborg et Blanken
2 CONC borg fratres et comites” confirmed “villam...Nuendorp” to Kloster Walkenried[978].  “Heinricus comes de Stalberch” confirmed that “frater suus comes Fridericus...cum...conjugis suæ Agnetis” had sold “decimam in Kaldenhusen” to Klo
2 CONC ster Walkenried by charter dated 22 Apr 1257[979].  “Henricus de Stalberch et Fredericus de Voxstede fratres comites” confirmed the donation of property “in villa Pesselde” to Kloster Walkenried by charter dated 20 May 1272[980]. 
2 CONC  '''married as her second husband, ADELHEID von Henneberg, widow of LOUIS [Ludwig] de Looz Graf von Rieneck, daughter of POPPO [VII] Graf von Henneberg & his first wife Elisabeth''' --- (-before 1259).  Her parentage and first mar
2 CONC riage are confirmed by the charter dated 1261 under which [her sons] “Ludewicus, Gerhardus et Heinricus fratres comites de Rienecke” protested the destruction of Schloß Esch, naming “avunculo nostro comite Hermanno de Hennenberg” 
2 CONC as mediator[981].  The chronology of her first husband indicates that Adelheid must have been born from her father’s first marriage.  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not been identified. 
2 CONT
