2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         '''HEINRICH''' (-Görz 24 Apr 1323, bur Treviso).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 9 Feb 1296 under which his mother "Grævinne Ofmey von Görtz" donated money, from the sale of her share in the inheritance
2 CONC  of Hardegg and Plain received from her brother, to "miner Tohter Offemeyn Claren", with the consent of "mines Herren und wirtes Graven Albrechts von Görtz und…siner eriben Grafen Heinriches und Grafen Albrechtes mines sunes"[1025
2 CONC ].  His birth from his father’s first marriage is confirmed by the following document: the 29 May 1275 marriage contract for his second marriage (between "Dominum Albertum comitem Goricie" and "dominam Offmyam…comitissam de Hardek
2 CONC ke", see below) specifies that “ipseque dominus Al. comes et filius suus quem habet ex alia domina uxore sua defuncta” would pay dowries to “filiam vel filias domine O. comitisse teneantur”[1026].  He succeeded his father in 1304 
2 CONC as HEINRICH III Graf von Görz.  Reichsvicar of Treviso 1311.  The Annales Foriulienses record the death "in festo sancti Georgii" in 1323 of "domnus Henricus comes Goriciæ" and his burial "in Tervisio"[1027].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m'''  /!\ firstly ([2 May] 1297) BEATRICE Ctss di Camerino, daughter of GHERARDO Conte di Camerino & his wife Chiara delle Torre (-1321 after 25 Aug). <br>  ''''/!\ Camino Veneto North Italy, NOT Camerino Marche center Italy /!
2 CONC \''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ( [1322] ) BEATRIX von Niederbayern, daughter of STEFAN I Duke of Lower Bavaria & his wife Jutta von Schweidnitz [Piast] (1302-Landshut 29 Apr 1360, bur Kloster Seligenthal).  Her marriage is deduced from the necr
2 CONC ology of Seligenthal which records the death "XVI Kal Apr" of "dominus Iohannes com de Görtze, filius domine Beatricis nobilis ducisse Bawarie"[1028].  Regent of Görz 1323-1326 and 1335-1338.  Regent of Treviso 1338.  The necrolog
2 CONC y of Seligenthal records the death "II Kal Mai 1340" of "domina Beatrix ducissa Bavarie et coma de Goerzen"[1029], although the year appears incorrect. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Graf Heinrich III & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT *a)         MEINHARD [V] (-after 21 Mar 1318). 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Graf Heinrich III & his second wife had one child: 
2 CONT *b)         JOHANN HEINRICH (-Trieste 17 Mar 1338).  He succeeded his father in 1323 as JOHANN HEINRICH Graf von Görz.  Reichsvicar of Treviso until 1329.  The necrology of Minoritenkirche, Vienna records the death "XVI Kal Mar" o
2 CONC f "Iohannes com Goritie"[1030].  The necrology of Seligenthal records the death "XVI Kal Apr" of "dominus Iohannes com de Görtze, filius domine Beatricis nobilis ducisse Bawarie"[1031].  m (29 Sep 1336) as her second husband, ANNA
2 CONC  of Austria, widow of HEINRICH III "der Natternberger" Duke of Bavaria in Niederbayern, daughter of FRIEDRICH I "dem Schönen" Duke of Austria & his wife Infanta doña Isabel de Aragón (1318-Vienna 14 Dec 1343, bur Vienna St Klara).
2 CONC   The primary source which confirms her first marriage has not so far been identified.  Nun at Convent of St Klara Vienna 1340, later Abbess.  The Necrologium Austriacum records the death "1343 XIX Kal Ian" of "Anna filia Frideric
2 CONC i regis Romanorum coma de Goertz", specifying that she entered "ordinem S Clare in Wienna" after the death of her husband, and her burial there[1032].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Graf Heinrich III had [three] illegitimate children by an unknown mistress: 
2 CONT *c)          ALZIBERTA .  m (1314) NIKOLAUS von Pramberg, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *d)         ELISABETH .  m OLIVIERO Sforza, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *e)         [AGNES .  m ALBERTO [II] della Scala Podestà di Verona, son of ALBOINO Della Scala & his second wife Beatrice di Corregio (-1352).] 
2 CONT
