1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_II_of_Gorizia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Albert II''' (died in 1327), a member of '''the House of Gorizia''' (Meinhardiner dynasty), ruled as governor of the County of Gorizia from 1323, on behalf of his nephew Count John Henry IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert II was a younger son of Count Albert I of Gorizia and his wife Euphemia, a daughter of the Silesian duke Konrad I of Głogów. He thereby was the younger brother of Henry III, ruling Count of Gorizia upon their father's death
2 CONC  in 1304. He inherited the lands in the Puster Valley. When his brother died in 1323, Albert acted as regent for Henry's minor son John Henry IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert married Elizabeth, a daughter of Landgrave Henry I of Hesse and, secondly, Euphemia of Mätsch, daughter of bailiff Ulrich II. He was the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Elizabeth, married Count Herman of Heunburg (d. 1322) and secondly Count William of Schaunberg-Trüchsen
2 CONT
2 CONT *Catherine, married Ulrich of Waldsee, who was Landeshauptmann of Styria
2 CONT
2 CONT *Clara, married Herdeggen of Pettau, field marshal of Styria
2 CONT
2 CONT *Catharina zu Neuhaus, married Ulrich of Taufers at Utenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT *Albert III (d. 1374)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Henry IV (d. 1361)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Meinhard VI (d. 1385)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert's three sons succeeded as Counts of Gorizia upon the early death of their cousin John Henry IV in 1338.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CARINTHIA.htm#AlbrechtIIIGorzLienzdied1327
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         '''ALBRECHT''' [III] (-[1325/27]).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 9 Feb 1296 under which his mother "Grævinne Ofmey von Görtz" donated money, from the sale of her share in the inheritance of Hardegg an
2 CONC d Plain received from her brother, to "miner Tohter Offemeyn Claren", with the consent of "mines Herren und wirtes Graven Albrechts von Görtz und…siner eriben Grafen Heinriches und Grafen Albrechtes mines sunes"[1033].  "Albertus…
2 CONC comes Goricie et Tyrolis, Aquilegiensis, Tridentine et Brixinensis ecclesiarum advocatus" confirmed donations to Tirol Neustift, with the consent of "domine Offemie consortis nostre", by charter dated 1313[1034].  He was regent of
2 CONC  Görz in 1323 for his nephew.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed (20 Feb 1283) to --- von Heunburg, daughter of ULRICH [II] Graf von Heunburg & his [second] wife Agnes von Baden.  The marriage contract between “Ulrich Graf von Heunburg...eine von unseren Töchtern” and “Albert dem edle
2 CONC n Grafen von Görz...seinem Sohne Albert, der er hat von seiner Gemahlin...Euphemia Gräfin von Ortenburg” is dated 20 Feb 1283[1035].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (contract 17 Mar 1299) ELISABETH von Hessen, daughter of HEINRICH I "das Kind" Fürst und Landgraf Herr von Hessen & his second wife Mechtild von Kleve (-after 30 Oct 1308).  The primary source which confirms her parentag
2 CONC e and marriage has not been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (before 1313) OFFMEI UTEHILD von Mätsch, daughter of ULRICH [II] Vogt von Mätsch & his wife Margareta von Vaz (-after 1353).  "Albertus…comes Goricie et Tyrolis, Aquilegiensis, Tridentine et Brixinensis ecclesiarum advo
2 CONC catus" confirmed donations to Tirol Neustift, with the consent of "domine Offemie consortis nostre", by charter dated 1313[1036].  She founded the Carmelite convent of Lienz in 1348[1037].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Albrecht [III] & his first wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ehe mit Euphemia von Ortenburg, beschrieben in: • Karlmann Tangl, Die Grafen von Ortenburg in Kärnten. Erste Abtheilung von 1058 bis 1256. in: Archiv für Kunde österreichischer Geschichts-Quellen 30/1, Wien 1863, S. 203–352.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
