0 @N6000000002187814251@ NOTE Henry III of Limburg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry III (c.1140 – 21 June 1221) was the duke of Limburg and count of Arlon from 1165 to his death. He was the son and successor of Henry II and Matilda of Saffenberg.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1172, he fought against the count of Luxembourg, Henry IV the Blind, and the his ally, the count of Hainault, Baldwin V. The environs of Arlon were devastated and the duke, overcome, had to recompense the count of Luxembourg fo
1 CONC r the wrongs he had done him. In 1183, he supported the election of Fulmar as archbishop of Trier. This was opposed by the Emperor Frederick Barbarossa.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry had to fight his nephew, Henry I of Brabant in connection with the advocacy of the abbey of Saint-Trond. The Brabantine duke claimed the advocacy as part of his mother's dowry. An arrangement put an end to the war in 1191 an
1 CONC d the duke of Limburg became a vassal of the duke of Brabant. The two dukes collaborated in the internal affairs of the region (Belgia).
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry later supported Otto of Brunswick over Philip of Swabia as German king and imperial claimant. He fought at the Battle of Bouvines in 1214. It was a disaster for Otto.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Henry II Duke of Limburg
1 CONT 1165–1221 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Waleran III 
1 CONT Count of Arlon
1 CONT 1165–1221 
