1 CONT Phillippe had arrived at Sicily prior to Richard, and in conjunction w ith Tancred prevented Eleanor d'Aquitaine and Berengaria from landing at Sicily and forced them to land instead at Brendisi.  While in Sicil y, Phillippe and R
1 CONC ichard quarreled endlessly.  Phillippe set sail fro m Sicily on 30 March 1191 for Palestine.  Phillippe landed with his tr oops in the environs of Acre on about 20 April 1191 at which time he t ook control of the army and began to
1 CONC  reorganize the faltering seige o f Leopold.  He was followed at the beginning of June 1191 by Richard t he Lionheart.  Phillippe, against Richards advice, put forward an atta ck on Acre which proved to be a failure and with that 
