1 CONT Phillippe, upon hearing of Richards death, proclaimed Arthur the right ful heir to England and the Angevin empire.  Phillippe marched west an d advanced on the area of Anjou and Maine.  Arthur of Brittany and hi s mother had march
1 CONC ed on Anjou and eventually made there way to LeMans .  By June of 1199, now King John had crossed the channel and landed i n the area of Dieppe.  Almost immediately there was a test of strengt h between Phillippe and John when Joh
1 CONC n besieged a castle in the area, but was quickly driven off.  By late 1199, a rift had developed betwee n Phillippe and Arthur of Brittany.  In late 1199, Phillippe and John - King of England concluded a five year truce by whcih P
1 CONC hillippe's so n Louis would marry one of John's Castillian's nieces.  John at the ti me had to return to England, so his then 71 year old mother Eleanor wa s sent to select the niece.  In mid January 1200, Phillippe was impose d w
1 CONC ith an interdict on his kingdom by the vatican to punish him fro hi s marital discrepancies.  On 22 May 1200, Phillippe and John of Englan d concluded the Treaty of Le Goulet which enshrined the terms of the p revious truce.  By i
