1 CONC erted his father's ducal rights. Godfrey and Henry e ntered into a war in which the latter was decisively and quickly destr oyed. Godfrey did not long enjoy his victory. He was killed by a disea se of the liver two years thence. H
1 CONC e was buried in the church of Saint -Pierre in Leuven.  He married Lutgard, daughter of Berengar II of Sul zbach and sister of Gertrude, wife of Conrad III of Germany, and Berth a, wife of Manuel I Comnenus, the emperor of Byzanti
1 CONC um. He was succeed ed by his son Godfrey III in both the counties and the duchy.
