0 @N6000000002187747407@ NOTE Margaret I, Countess of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret I of Alsace (died November 15, 1194) was countess of Flanders from 1191 to her death.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the daughter of Thierry, Count of Flanders and Sibylla of Anjou, and the heiress of her childless brother, Philip of Flanders.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1169 she married Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut, who became her co-ruler. They had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Isabelle of Hainaut (Valenciennes, April 1170 – March 15, 1190, Paris), married king Philip II of France
1 CONT     * Baldwin VI of Hainaut (1171–1205), also count of Flanders and Latin Emperor
1 CONT     * Yolanda of Flanders (1175–1219), married Peter of Courtenay, Latin Emperor
1 CONT     * Philip I, Marquis of Namur (1175–1212)
1 CONT     * Henry of Flanders (1176–1216), Latin Emperor
1 CONT     * Sybille (1179 – January 9, 1217), married c. 1197 Guichard IV, Sire de Beaujeu (d. 1216)
1 CONT     * Eustace of Hainault (d. 1219), regent of the Kingdom of Thessalonica
1 CONT     * Godfrey of Hainault
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Philip Count of Flanders
1 CONT 1191–1194
1 CONT with Baldwin VIII (1191–1194) Succeeded by
1 CONT Baldwin VIII
