1 CONC they crossed through. Theyarrived at Constantinople by December of 1146, ahead of the Frencharmy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Rather than taking the coastal road around Anatolia throughChristian-held territory, by which he sent most of his noncombatants,Conrad took his army straight across Anatolia. On October 25, 1147,they lost a major battle to the Tur
1 CONC ks at Dorylaeum. Conrad and most ofthe mounted knights escaped, but most of the foot soldiers were killedor captured. Conrad eventually reached the crusader kingdom by seafrom Constantinople.
